[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4845966-372c-548d-a64a-8d5c7c19d0ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453580} {:answer/id #uuid "f1849a3b-58bc-5f4a-b012-a58f9871612b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4845966-372c-548d-a64a-8d5c7c19d0ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453580} :answer-field/id #uuid "d47284cf-891c-5cb8-ba28-4824c46e48a5" :answer-field/key "${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(c)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454540} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e37544ac-2fca-57be-8001-9189226db946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453582} {:answer/id #uuid "70351b57-7f19-5fbe-be03-fa7da2c1b679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70351b57-7f19-5fbe-be03-fa7da2c1b679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453583} :answer-field/id #uuid "69249cbb-7e3c-531b-bd6d-21bc466588de" :answer-field/key "${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(c)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454541} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "433a72ab-7d38-5e4a-8f83-e3fe8097b4f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453584} {:answer/id #uuid "09e2b953-fb38-58ce-a5b6-d43d2e3d4354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "433a72ab-7d38-5e4a-8f83-e3fe8097b4f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453584} :answer-field/id #uuid "e58739c5-1889-5e03-9e74-ee19d0f13dfc" :answer-field/key "$c\\in A\\cap B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10dc60fb-f25e-52f7-9f87-59ad72f93d31" :question/math-academy-id "q-174392" :question/problem "$$\n{1}_{A}(c)=0,\\,{1}_{B}(c)=1\n$$\n\nGiven the values of the indicator functions of the sets $A$ and $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(c)=1$ is false while statement ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(c)=0$ is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(c) & =min{{1}_{A}(c),{1}_{B}(c)} \\\\  & =min{0,1} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement $c\\in A\\cap B$ is false. Since ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(c)=0,$ we conclude that $c$ does not belong to $A\\cap B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(c)=0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376707 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203911 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5725601-8181-582a-935d-d3dfde851d63" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Functional Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7fc041e-c282-53eb-a8fb-17683d9e91b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471371} {:answer/id #uuid "6bbff658-86dd-56c3-85fb-1774d488ff70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7fc041e-c282-53eb-a8fb-17683d9e91b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471371} :answer-field/id #uuid "78749954-9c82-5d36-aec7-fd4ea8273546" :answer-field/key "$x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x={y}^{2},$ defined on $R$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472191} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63b147bd-19f2-51fc-bc81-f4a381a9136b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471373} {:answer/id #uuid "a5356e06-be98-5dcc-9cf5-65fdd6f7ee01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5356e06-be98-5dcc-9cf5-65fdd6f7ee01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471374} :answer-field/id #uuid "41342172-0d32-5257-82bd-9001c09a991c" :answer-field/key "$x\\,S\\,y$ if and only if $x{y}^{3}=1,$ defined on ${R}^{+}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d524e9f7-3941-5d66-8a06-46fbe008780d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471375} {:answer/id #uuid "0542e442-4632-53a4-a7fa-0a4416f29cab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d524e9f7-3941-5d66-8a06-46fbe008780d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471375} :answer-field/id #uuid "c209c1d3-98a7-5e7d-b998-6962a694bfb2" :answer-field/key "$x\\,T\\,y$ if and only if $y∣2x,$ defined on $Z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bd2e7ad1-df50-507b-b322-c68735f660cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-216886" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are functional?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R$ defined over $A$ and $B$ is *functional* (or a *partial function*) if, for all $a\\in A$ and ${b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\in B,$ we have \n\n$$\n(a,{b}_{1})\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(a,{b}_{2})\\in R\\,⇒\\,{b}_{1}={b}_{2}.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if the first components of two ordered pairs are equal, then the second components must also be equal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations.\n\n- $R$ is *not* functional. Notice that $1={1}^{2}$ and $1=(-1)^{2}.$ So, $R$ contains pairs $(1,1)$ and $(1,-1)$ with the same first component but different second components.\n\n- $S$ is functional. Indeed, $a{b}_{1}^{3}=1$ and $a{b}_{2}^{3}=1$ is equivalent to ${b}_{1}={b}_{2}$ over ${R}^{+}.$ So, when the first components of two pairs are equal, then the second components are also equal.\n\n- $T$ is *not* functional. Notice that $2∣2(3)$ and $3∣2(3).$ So, $T$ contains pairs $(3,2)$ and $(3,3)$ with the same first component but different second components.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$S$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69b456ea-44de-59f0-b2c8-bc5b9495974f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87e9b7a8-66bb-5d09-bd58-7f87a8bd1e23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471453} {:answer/id #uuid "e97876f9-dc61-5e39-8076-e12233f6be8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87e9b7a8-66bb-5d09-bd58-7f87a8bd1e23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471453} :answer-field/id #uuid "8280f47e-8f45-599c-bff2-457d358b2b6a" :answer-field/key "$A$ is an interior point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472232} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f72681b-5388-5ed3-af01-b1576e6f61e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471455} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d0bd01-3ea0-5efa-8d77-62f3532e9944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7d0bd01-3ea0-5efa-8d77-62f3532e9944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471456} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae5ad6b4-ee02-5fd9-aab5-6a8880027d51" :answer-field/key "$B$ is a boundary point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472233} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99dde3fb-5ec8-5777-87bd-ade4d80c1969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471457} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a22ad6-93c9-579f-a9f6-63ef19bcd4ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99dde3fb-5ec8-5777-87bd-ade4d80c1969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471457} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b60aa23-b672-5281-b5ed-2e35c18d69b6" :answer-field/key "$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10cee0d6-c023-521a-a779-cab7a62d3b8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-64999" :question/problem "![](images/7f/7ffcda47f0d750ce9f25e50b0b28091ff4279467313fbe604eac0fc9b1229806.png)\n\nConsider the set $M,$ depicted by the shaded region above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is less than $\\delta .$\n\n$$\n\\{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta \\}\n$$\n\nIn two-dimensional space, a neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is the open disc $|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a6c72e169f3104eb0b9958673cc6644f770e6bcc3ebf23360eb20189325a28.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/08/080d6cf1cd468b7ddfe65df2e6a21792e1afe470ddd571c6b5ec25569d1fb537.png)\n\n- Statement “$A$ is an interior point of the set $M$” is false. Every open neighborhood of $A$ contains points that belong to \n$M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$ The point $A$ is a boundary point for the given set.\n\n- Statement “$B$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” is true. The point $B$ is a boundary point because every open neighborhood of $B$ contains points that belong to $M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$\n\n- Statement “$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” is false. Indeed, $C$ is an interior point since there exists an open neighborhood of $C$ that is fully contained inside the set $M.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is '“$B$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” only'."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69b456ea-44de-59f0-b2c8-bc5b9495974f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce141660-9bda-5acc-9a0b-31d41347e2bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471477} {:answer/id #uuid "287b6d72-9962-57e1-a9da-dfee2551628f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "287b6d72-9962-57e1-a9da-dfee2551628f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471478} :answer-field/id #uuid "be4caeae-3a30-5feb-a2cf-5a156c3f7974" :answer-field/key "$A$ is an interior point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472244} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38a73300-641f-5407-b3f4-8f357fe85d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471479} {:answer/id #uuid "15d9b14e-9a66-5c4f-b212-9a4c1df2304c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38a73300-641f-5407-b3f4-8f357fe85d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471479} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdc78f53-2967-5895-a127-2e9edae5311a" :answer-field/key "$B$ is a boundary point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09e5c543-06f6-52de-8da5-ae1935d181e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471481} {:answer/id #uuid "07d213c4-b711-5570-9c3b-bec90c86c6d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07d213c4-b711-5570-9c3b-bec90c86c6d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471482} :answer-field/id #uuid "85cd195a-49d4-5f8f-83a9-a08d3f58048b" :answer-field/key "$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "afb4c2fe-2048-5475-a89e-bbe7b7062429" :question/math-academy-id "q-71689" :question/problem "![](images/94/94911d7be45c5572a4ce47ce95c81a66bf6276144eeace8dd74cac15646c2082.png)\n\nConsider the set $M,$ depicted by the shaded region above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is less than $\\delta .$\n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nIn two-dimensional space, a neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is the open disc $|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a6c72e169f3104eb0b9958673cc6644f770e6bcc3ebf23360eb20189325a28.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/50/5024d8cf4c7a21667eb91dadee2d3368f1f9f3504e2a06f27b020c2d18804586.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is an interior point of the set $M$” is true. Indeed, $A$ is an interior point since there exists an open neighborhood of $A$ that is fully contained inside the set $M.$\n\n- Statement “$B$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” is false. There exists an open neighborhood of $B$ that is fully contained inside the set $M.$\n\n- Statement “$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” is true. Indeed, every open neighborhood of $C$ contains points that belong to $M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$ The point $C$ is a boundary point for the given set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is '“$A$ is an interior point of the set $M$” and “$C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$” only'."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377668 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Given a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dbd8a41-022e-505a-9a23-5897ee2615d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453946} {:answer/id #uuid "e964dc82-e823-526c-bb4e-d9d86b715c3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dbd8a41-022e-505a-9a23-5897ee2615d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453946} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd5d2420-05be-505d-a6da-9370564b875a" :answer-field/key "$A$ is **not** invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454723} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bfaf3e3-c8c3-5b0f-905a-7cfc3c188946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453948} {:answer/id #uuid "8e7b77cf-0808-52a0-92c8-aef31c85857a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e7b77cf-0808-52a0-92c8-aef31c85857a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453949} :answer-field/id #uuid "b912caf2-b2fa-5b75-b5a5-849cbfd33c40" :answer-field/key "The lines $2x-3y=1$ and $2x-2y=2$ intersect at exactly one point" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454724} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "581a4ee7-2ef6-5d6a-8a10-f2e80e510c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453950} {:answer/id #uuid "b85c6ec3-9718-5d84-925f-86b8f81442df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "581a4ee7-2ef6-5d6a-8a10-f2e80e510c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453950} :answer-field/id #uuid "74197001-61cf-522e-acb4-234d12a1ff07" :answer-field/key "$Ax=0$ has no solution" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454725}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aafb0544-5c12-5527-bc2a-2417215aad99" :question/math-academy-id "q-73566" :question/problem "Let \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-2)-(-3)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. \n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is **not** invertible” is false by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement “The lines $2x-3y=1$ and $2x-2y=2$ intersect at exactly one point” is true by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement “$Ax=0$ has no solution” is false since, according to the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, the system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\nTherefore, only statement “The lines $2x-3y=1$ and $2x-2y=2$ intersect at exactly one point” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377763 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee3ba979-73eb-55d9-98be-53eb63f15310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454018} {:answer/id #uuid "42f7e70e-a33c-5389-83b8-4b66c4b40413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42f7e70e-a33c-5389-83b8-4b66c4b40413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454019} :answer-field/id #uuid "51beb1c0-c434-5ffe-be4f-d1af3a966f94" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454759} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b27c5d69-4610-55e4-befd-bab1f9f21b77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454020} {:answer/id #uuid "7f38039b-9493-5449-afe0-51512728ff71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f38039b-9493-5449-afe0-51512728ff71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454021} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bd2f4dc-0220-560a-b969-e0fb63f01a28" :answer-field/key "$A$ is not  invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22168706-fdd0-5ec9-8357-a478a254b0de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454022} {:answer/id #uuid "b3eaef39-5ed2-5d0e-8448-e5d92a445686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22168706-fdd0-5ec9-8357-a478a254b0de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454022} :answer-field/id #uuid "447c453c-9c02-53db-ad8b-23d0593303f4" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c7ff497-8845-5d34-a5a1-e0b10d7a1e25" :question/math-academy-id "q-79367" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix with $3$ pivot columns?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=5=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ is true. Indeed, since $A$ has $3$ pivot columns, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is not  invertible” is true. Indeed, for the matrix $A,$ the number of the columns is $n=5.$ Now, since $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$ is false. According to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-3 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{rank}(A)=3$; “$A$ is not  invertible” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d48f791-cfb2-5905-8a08-ac3a02cb98d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471651} {:answer/id #uuid "42a831ec-5eee-5950-80a9-6df9cae47ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42a831ec-5eee-5950-80a9-6df9cae47ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471652} :answer-field/id #uuid "895886fe-f51a-5925-af30-4f44e0e9cea8" :answer-field/key "$¬(A∧¬B)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472331} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b947d56e-0ddb-51a5-b1b0-2e3173f580d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471653} {:answer/id #uuid "dde7200c-ebbb-5580-81f9-9955e8fa6c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b947d56e-0ddb-51a5-b1b0-2e3173f580d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471653} :answer-field/id #uuid "34007ef7-681a-5401-838e-6a9b5d455f4d" :answer-field/key "$¬A∧B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472332} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bc9cb5e-96ad-5a73-89b4-b5349f290448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471655} {:answer/id #uuid "ec42fe8c-f2e7-5cb5-b521-a55d198bc728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec42fe8c-f2e7-5cb5-b521-a55d198bc728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471656} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb5177ea-d86a-50ce-ba4e-14b59e4673a4" :answer-field/key "$¬A∨B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e6dc3a9-8bf9-5ff1-b677-65bc92bbe439" :question/math-academy-id "q-81483" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∧¬B)\\,$ | $\\,¬A∧B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∨B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬(A∧¬B)$ and $¬A∨B$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $¬(A∧¬B)$; $¬A∨B$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ca8340a-82df-55a3-9305-a651afdc38de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471663} {:answer/id #uuid "b512a5e7-a7fe-581c-9548-feb54ed21083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ca8340a-82df-55a3-9305-a651afdc38de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471663} :answer-field/id #uuid "22724fc6-7046-54cf-a41e-738bcd859a57" :answer-field/key "$¬(X∧¬Y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472337} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "329d9332-b9ec-5c45-91cc-764d05e4ac3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471665} {:answer/id #uuid "dcecd39b-b8b6-5c5a-9566-8a787a0b5d12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471666}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcecd39b-b8b6-5c5a-9566-8a787a0b5d12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471666} :answer-field/id #uuid "636ea43f-5ead-5d01-924e-a90998dbf93d" :answer-field/key "$¬(X∨¬Y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472338} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "860cc7cf-c716-518d-a03f-8318830755b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471667} {:answer/id #uuid "0fde2323-d58a-51c0-94ed-e6ef42732655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fde2323-d58a-51c0-94ed-e6ef42732655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471668} :answer-field/id #uuid "db297399-8cfe-5660-9270-43f76ee3571e" :answer-field/key "$¬X∧Y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472339}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6020d90d-05af-58b3-8eac-fa53d62d19da" :question/math-academy-id "q-81486" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∧¬Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨¬Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬X∧Y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬(X∨¬Y)$ and $¬X∧Y$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $¬(X∨¬Y)$; $¬X∧Y$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64a3922f-7e74-562f-9bb9-c4a41e912ce7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Conditional Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "382b0e40-0b72-5c5c-9d94-193493c39204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471687} {:answer/id #uuid "ce73943b-79af-5cb9-8def-b3e711d8e0d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "382b0e40-0b72-5c5c-9d94-193493c39204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471687} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb80344b-80bc-5f25-8430-2d5d6bd787bb" :answer-field/key "**If** $2$ is an even number, **then** $8$ is a prime number." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472349} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "120d3451-1808-58bd-a146-10d1068008fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471689} {:answer/id #uuid "161c51b2-8820-5a19-8c55-8c44271bd04d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "161c51b2-8820-5a19-8c55-8c44271bd04d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471690} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c0a9c54-4abd-51b2-8613-c8fac1cc2414" :answer-field/key "**If** $8$ is an even number, **then** $2$ is an even number." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472350} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "677cd23a-a88e-5e97-a475-ca256aa1f1bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471691} {:answer/id #uuid "f7dfca88-d58d-5326-958d-bb7cbc86b71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7dfca88-d58d-5326-958d-bb7cbc86b71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471692} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca18faec-5ae3-50f0-af6d-fa9045deca1b" :answer-field/key "**If** $8$ is a prime number, **then** $2$ is an even number." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28c545f7-d207-5c17-a488-3a5f17bee359" :question/math-academy-id "q-82071" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement “**If** $2$ is an even number, **then** $8$ is a prime number” is false. The antecedent \"$2$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$8$ is a prime number\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement “**If** $8$ is an even number, **then** $2$ is an even number” is true. The antecedent \"$8$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$2$ is an even number\" is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement “**If** $8$ is a prime number, **then** $2$ is an even number” is true. The antecedent \"$8$ is a prime number\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “**If** $8$ is an even number, **then** $2$ is an even number”; “**If** $8$ is a prime number, **then** $2$ is an even number” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377872 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64a3922f-7e74-562f-9bb9-c4a41e912ce7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Conditional Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ebdb5b2-a035-5e73-b3a5-fea90ac2c5f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471693} {:answer/id #uuid "4bcf4f12-388d-5ee8-afa1-ccb824f1a67f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bcf4f12-388d-5ee8-afa1-ccb824f1a67f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471694} :answer-field/id #uuid "0588cda6-3fc3-547c-bc04-d152f8cd51a6" :answer-field/key "**If** $7$ is divisible by $2$, **then** $8$ is divisible by $4.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472352} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "771c7caf-77a6-5631-b98f-7c73465b1733" 