4c31-c35d-57df-a0ce-02370148728a" :question/math-academy-id "q-82089" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement “**If** $2+3<4,$ **then** $1+5<8.$” is true. The antecedent $2+3<4$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement “**If** $1+5<8,$ **then** $2+3<4.$” is false. The antecedent $1+5<8$ is true, and the consequent $2+3<4$ is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement “**If** $1+5<4,$ **then** $2+3<8.$” is true. Again, the antecedent $1+5<4$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “**If** $2+3<4,$ **then** $1+5<8.$”; “**If** $1+5<4,$ **then** $2+3<8.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157293 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "281873c8-e173-5181-8281-96b84d636b3c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About the Chinese Remainder Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbbe17e2-2245-5b19-baca-5456adac09aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471765} {:answer/id #uuid "08a66943-735d-5f31-9404-bb573f0d4a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbbe17e2-2245-5b19-baca-5456adac09aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471765} :answer-field/id #uuid "deb55755-746d-562f-9818-8bd362ec525c" :answer-field/key "$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x≡4 & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\ x≡5 & (\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\\right.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472388} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33afde02-6c00-5acc-b627-671a3dd3be13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471767} {:answer/id #uuid "30552bbd-ad0a-50b5-ab48-2ca1fc8d73e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30552bbd-ad0a-50b5-ab48-2ca1fc8d73e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471768} :answer-field/id #uuid "0554ea35-bbf0-5e21-bd1a-586d4cd5d745" :answer-field/key "$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x≡2 & (\\text{mod}\\,3) \\\\ x≡14 & (\\text{mod}\\,16)\\end{aligned}\\right.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472389} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e90c9bb9-0a65-5aa4-92c8-378c3f722004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471769} {:answer/id #uuid "5231270d-8208-54ce-9a8e-aedfc4af4fd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e90c9bb9-0a65-5aa4-92c8-378c3f722004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471769} :answer-field/id #uuid "82ef0c81-c876-58a1-8875-d6aaea32054e" :answer-field/key "$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x≡3 & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\ x≡7 & (\\text{mod}\\,12)\\end{aligned}\\right.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b00b20e-2b69-5a9e-a153-226cf102bd50" :question/math-academy-id "q-83978" :question/problem "According to the Chinese remainder theorem, which of the following systems of congruences has a unique solution modulo $48?$ \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The Chinese remainder theorem states that if the natural numbers ${n}_{1},{n}_{2},…,{n}_{k}$ are pairwise coprime, meaning that $\\text{gcd}({n}_{i},{n}_{j})=1$ whenever $i\\ne j,$ then for any integers ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},…,{a}_{k}$ the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x≡{a}_{1} & (\\text{mod}\\,{n}_{1}) \\\\ x≡{a}_{2} & (\\text{mod}\\,{n}_{2}) \\\\ \\,⋮ \\\\ x≡{a}_{k} & (\\text{mod}\\,{n}_{k})\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nhas a unique solution modulo ${n}_{1}{n}_{2}⋯{n}_{k}.$\n\nLet's now inspect each of the given systems in turn.\n\n- The theorem does *not* apply to system $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x≡4 & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\ x≡5 & (\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\\right.$ since $6$ and $8$ are not coprime: \n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(6,8)=2>1\n$$\n\n- The theorem applies to system $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x≡2 & (\\text{mod}\\,3) \\\\ x≡14 & (\\text{mod}\\,16)\\end{aligned}\\right.$. The numbers $3,$ and $16$ are pairwise coprime natural numbers. Therefore, according to the Chinese remainder theorem, the system has a unique solution modulo $3\\cdot 16=48.$\n\n- The theorem does *not* apply to system $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x≡3 & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\ x≡7 & (\\text{mod}\\,12)\\end{aligned}\\right.$ since $4$ and $12$ are not coprime: \n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(4,12)=4>1\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x≡2 & (\\text{mod}\\,3) \\\\ x≡14 & (\\text{mod}\\,16)\\end{aligned}\\right.$ only"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377969 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c290820-a094-51ac-84b5-47702a109966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471771} {:answer/id #uuid "5e9124fe-1470-5337-aa89-5154e8ad7638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c290820-a094-51ac-84b5-47702a109966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471771} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb804d1c-5844-5bb6-9474-5a626bd3017a" :answer-field/key "$¬(¬X∧¬Y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472391} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ae3d2de-d895-5503-8bf5-477e4cd8f480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471773} {:answer/id #uuid "5a33ccc0-89e2-571b-8c14-1c066339a00e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a33ccc0-89e2-571b-8c14-1c066339a00e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471774} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1f21ad2-346a-5efd-9af6-80034699cb49" :answer-field/key "$¬X∨¬Y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472392} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "468d83f5-0c5a-509d-883e-66c99ea663ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471775} {:answer/id #uuid "0222d302-0120-53ed-b7e8-a1a6af1d2b8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0222d302-0120-53ed-b7e8-a1a6af1d2b8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471776} :answer-field/id #uuid "20444d96-a20e-51cc-9ba0-b0767933578a" :answer-field/key "$¬(X∧Y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4951a3e-3ef9-5319-bbf9-d2c571b3026e" :question/math-academy-id "q-86684" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(¬X∧¬Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬X∨¬Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∧Y)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬X∨¬Y$ and $¬(X∧Y)$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $¬X∨¬Y$; $¬(X∧Y)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cadf2b3a-2887-51a1-ac9a-6a100a720148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471777} {:answer/id #uuid "13acb438-be49-5b43-9f6b-58f9715282b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13acb438-be49-5b43-9f6b-58f9715282b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471778} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5593c75-ada1-59d7-8a43-cb5af290a565" :answer-field/key "$¬X∧(X∨¬Y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472394} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d234654d-a06c-5b98-870a-02f1f2e9cf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471779} {:answer/id #uuid "f29aac37-329c-5783-b10b-4b6a4d478e56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d234654d-a06c-5b98-870a-02f1f2e9cf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471779} :answer-field/id #uuid "13849d25-31be-5849-8b24-d650f4eb32c6" :answer-field/key "$¬X∨(X∧¬Y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472395} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "263de33c-6795-58ce-85ae-92a97254075c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471781} {:answer/id #uuid "47908abc-c854-5546-bdc1-39309bb92cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47908abc-c854-5546-bdc1-39309bb92cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471782} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca92a53d-50d7-5e4b-8ec5-4c9924570bd9" :answer-field/key "$¬(X∨(¬X∧Y))$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "17f91135-f9d8-56cf-88b5-eaf7c61a4e5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-86690" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬X∧(X∨¬Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬X∨(X∧¬Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨(¬X∧Y))\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬X∧(X∨¬Y)$ and $¬(X∨(¬X∧Y))$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $¬X∧(X∨¬Y)$; $¬(X∨(¬X∧Y))$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8e517c4-23a1-5dc9-9873-db08b9aeb3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470649} {:answer/id #uuid "9ade5b3f-5cb6-518d-a651-81454cda6151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8e517c4-23a1-5dc9-9873-db08b9aeb3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470649} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8c841ea-fba3-56e1-9d85-327679542b1d" :answer-field/key "$F∧(F∨E)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471830} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d934691-3b6b-5ec3-9db2-a20903a11180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470651} {:answer/id #uuid "e81df654-954c-56c2-9696-9eb3a8423750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e81df654-954c-56c2-9696-9eb3a8423750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470652} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a871827-a4f1-5907-9569-c6ab0b678ac6" :answer-field/key "$E∧(F∨E)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471831} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "955b841d-027f-5c52-87ad-2ca861b76788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470653} {:answer/id #uuid "57651c46-a371-5c02-83b4-7068e2870cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "955b841d-027f-5c52-87ad-2ca861b76788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470653} :answer-field/id #uuid "28bd83f8-cec3-591f-af68-2513445eddd0" :answer-field/key "$E∨(F∨E)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3546d6ca-c236-59ab-90e2-5cf833951b0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-103060" :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $E?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The law that conjunction absorbs disjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nE∧(E∨F)≡E.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement $F∧(F∨E)$ is *not* logically equivalent to $E.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F∧(F∨E) & ≡F≢E.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement $E∧(F∨E)$ is logically equivalent to $E.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E∧(F∨E) & ≡E∧(E∨F) \\\\  & ≡E.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement $E∨(F∨E)$ is *not* logically equivalent to $E.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $E∧(F∨E)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378188 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a897efcf-c493-5598-9acc-bff660f4510e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470655} {:answer/id #uuid "0355f714-2a1a-5862-bd5e-c5aa32745c3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0355f714-2a1a-5862-bd5e-c5aa32745c3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470656} :answer-field/id #uuid "73d99ea3-1208-5bf6-b85d-273ae3953352" :answer-field/key "$(H∨G)∧G$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17b35f02-1aef-5b21-a202-ba62dbfbfef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470657} {:answer/id #uuid "68bac85e-4e35-5a79-a210-515b38fc270c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17b35f02-1aef-5b21-a202-ba62dbfbfef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470657} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1a78e23-b7a6-556b-863b-65847687283d" :answer-field/key "$H∧(H∨G)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471834} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b810de89-26a4-5c34-8c1b-e6d776e941a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470659} {:answer/id #uuid "737bbab7-f434-550f-aebd-27c4ad66b423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b810de89-26a4-5c34-8c1b-e6d776e941a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470659} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7b00160-674f-5206-919d-5ba05b820cb7" :answer-field/key "$(G∨H)∨G$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "897313ab-8a44-5c6f-bd61-a0fa12f9c240" :question/math-academy-id "q-103062" :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $G?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The law that conjunction absorbs disjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nG∧(G∨H)≡G.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement $(H∨G)∧G$ is logically equivalent to $G.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(H∨G)∧G & ≡G∧(H∨G) \\\\  & ≡G∧(G∨H) \\\\  & ≡G.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement $H∧(H∨G)$ is *not* logically equivalent to $G.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}H∧(H∨G) & ≡H≢G.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement $(G∨H)∨G$ is *not* logically equivalent to $G.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $(H∨G)∧G$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb6e0931-7b46-55a9-aedc-7e3c239f2548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470661} {:answer/id #uuid "93e7930e-b8e0-5b4e-9f37-e812ddbbf78e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb6e0931-7b46-55a9-aedc-7e3c239f2548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470661} :answer-field/id #uuid "eac6cee7-69ab-56c7-aabd-58768c438222" :answer-field/key "$¬B∧(A∨¬B)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471836} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c34c016-0f66-57ab-a126-a