ch of the given statements.\n\n- Statement $¬B∧(A∨¬B)$ is *not* logically equivalent to $A.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬B∧(A∨¬B) & ≡¬B∧(¬B∨A) \\\\  & ≡¬B≢A.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement $(¬B∨A)∧A$ is logically equivalent to $A.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(¬B∨A)∧A & ≡A∧(¬B∨A) \\\\  & ≡A∧(A∨¬B) \\\\  & ≡A.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement $A∧(¬B∨A)$ is logically equivalent to $A.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∧(¬B∨A) & ≡A∧(A∨¬B) \\\\  & ≡A.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $(¬B∨A)∧A$; $A∧(¬B∨A)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378202 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a792c1a6-9640-5fad-85b2-fd8f2540a5f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470667} {:answer/id #uuid "5c170663-9340-5394-81f4-bdd17320b665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a792c1a6-9640-5fad-85b2-fd8f2540a5f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470667} :answer-field/id #uuid "df01b8a6-dd41-5f50-96ae-767d85aada7e" :answer-field/key "$¬D∧(C∧¬D)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18f4bdbf-7cdb-54ec-8df5-0062b6ec5b31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470669} {:answer/id #uuid "e569d768-21a6-56ee-bfba-487c7d6a9866" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.typ