 :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "957e916a-1a46-5f09-b0b4-71f6f746df0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-104666" :question/problem "![](images/ca/ca165438c64994306acd6031d5f8e5a0e6d4d0d11a5f6fea8097b19f5105438c.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The function has a jump discontinuity at $x=3.$ Checking our conditions, we see that\n\n- $f(3)=-1$ exists, $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)$ does not exist $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo the second condition failed. It failed because the left and right-sided limits are not equal:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}f(x)=-1,\\,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}f(x)=3.\n$$\n\nThese limits both exist and are finite, yet they are not equal. Therefore, the discontinuity at $x=3$ is a jump discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, “It has a jump discontinuity at $x=3$” is true, and “It has a removable discontinuity at $x=3$” and “It is continuous at $x=3$” are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e476a7e6-9fe8-5985-ab3d-474e04a7980c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470829} {:answer/id #uuid "7af1392e-9bfd-5650-b6c7-cc5983449290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e476a7e6-9fe8-5985-ab3d-474e04a7980c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470829} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aa6ab55-2c08-50d9-8d9e-4dda3b96a9e4" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }3x+y<8,\\\\\\,0<x<3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471920} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fbbc87e-3691-52f5-8ce4-c5cbaad6b748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470831} {:answer/id #uuid "7e31bb92-ac20-5fe1-8af7-bc33a8b119a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e31bb92-ac20-5fe1-8af7-bc33a8b119a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470832} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e97e70a-fdb0-5789-bc5d-9049a1c4f9c7" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }0\\le x<6,\\\\\\,2<y\\le 4\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471921} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16a2cecd-883c-5851-be4b-db3c4e83d69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470833} {:answer/id #uuid "2b94ed74-766b-54f1-92b2-f5c251317f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16a2cecd-883c-5851-be4b-db3c4e83d69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470833} :answer-field/id #uuid "97b3b63f-64f6-53e3-a996-0684f567a58b" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}<6\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c082af6c-4b35-55f0-b925-7876243430ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-105443" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(0,3).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(3,2).$\n\n- The third set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }0\\le x<6,\\\\\\,2<y\\le 4\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e3f425a-0a1f-515b-8c03-990715e116f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470835} {:answer/id #uuid "46c61006-9d69-5224-84b5-adb4594d575a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46c61006-9d69-5224-84b5-adb4594d575a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470836} :answer-field/id #uuid "c24fe181-c890-5457-b487-5bd9845a29a6" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,6\\le x<9,\\\\\\,0<y<2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471923} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "455ea2d6-36ea-506e-8abc-4fb2725d1508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470837} {:answer/id #uuid "b1bbc0e3-f77f-5075-b7c1-c24869a40657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "455ea2d6-36ea-506e-8abc-4fb2725d1508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470837} :answer-field/id #uuid "523aebc4-d33b-5507-8bcd-9a008fe77b20" :answer-field/key "${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471924} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a53fe6cb-2b4e-5db2-a7b8-cf233dd5a07f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470839} {:answer/id #uuid "0c743f3a-ed2f-55ac-b5d2-1af41de6baef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a53fe6cb-2b4e-5db2-a7b8-cf233dd5a07f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470839} :answer-field/id #uuid "39ebafac-d103-5f82-9a2a-34326808b7f4" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}<3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f4b0cdf-9fe1-57d6-a009-4edf0331d401" :question/math-academy-id "q-105444" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(6,1).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(8,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\n- The third set is also *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,6\\le x<9,\\\\\\,0<y<2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ee869f7-f725-5bde-a20f-d84176a57341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470847} {:answer/id #uuid "1d73b7d4-fe5d-5d31-9705-14e5c7ac2ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d73b7d4-fe5d-5d31-9705-14e5c7ac2ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470848} :answer-field/id #uuid "8443cc6b-4590-53c1-ba28-2262ff94d030" :answer-field/key "If the sky is clear, then you do not need an umbrella." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471929} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "283e20ae-0701-5835-9917-a74613735477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470849} {:answer/id #uuid "5d48533d-df16-55a3-bd09-809c8c4e5b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "283e20ae-0701-5835-9917-a74613735477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470849} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b626c8a-c307-5508-bb16-8c0338464c78" :answer-field/key "If you do not need an umbrella, then the sky is clear." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471930} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d09b2211-9c73-5892-89f2-b1430f6074f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470851} {:answer/id #uuid "ceb04f59-6b8b-5f39-bd06-0bc33298c2f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d09b2211-9c73-5892-89f2-b1430f6074f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470851} :answer-field/id #uuid "89f298f8-84db-55c2-ac60-1d92591515e0" :answer-field/key "If the sky is not clear, then you need an umbrella." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4da29991-8f92-54a5-9016-f20e2647e29f" :question/math-academy-id "q-106802" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** you need an umbrella, **then** the sky is not clear.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive.\n\n- Statement “If the sky is clear, then you do not need an umbrella” is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement “If you do not need an umbrella, then the sky is clear” is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement “If the sky is not clear, then you need an umbrella” is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If the sky is clear, then you do not need an umbrella” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "913e0931-a878-5504-b8b6-00f819edf9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453210} {:answer/id #uuid "461ff5c7-f262-59e0-9e6a-5ccd795fb660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "913e0931-a878-5504-b8b6-00f819edf9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453210} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e294ac2-b715-5c6e-b139-8e2b8b489e3a" :answer-field/key "$S$ is closed under matrix addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454355} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e10c2846-bfa3-5599-a565-ba95e776088c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453212} {:answer/id #uuid "dfd1227a-6d81-5364-a894-22a85a885507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfd1227a-6d81-5364-a894-22a85a885507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453213} :answer-field/id #uuid "5eca9126-955c-5afe-833c-fc32a0b53bb9" :answer-field/key "$S$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "076b77e2-6bf3-5918-86f9-98829053c98d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453214} {:answer/id #uuid "d46b15b3-6f74-5c05-b218-76f6180d184c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "076b77e2-6bf3-5918-86f9-98829053c98d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453214} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab876604-ae7b-5692-8d5d-ac2e83bc51d1" :answer-field/key "$S$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454357} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a38d2c4-5da1-58d9-ad2f-9024e96c37be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453216} {:answer/id #uuid "9261a407-a47e-58cf-876d-d1ebb17244ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9261a407-a47e-58cf-876d-d1ebb17244ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453217} :answer-field/id #uuid "5823a91a-8b7b-550d-a8ed-1b40a6c306e7" :answer-field/key "$S$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29e169b1-20c5-5789-9178-14e4b85ea9c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-107117" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R,$ and its subset $S$ containing $2\\times 2$ matrices that are not invertible. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement “$S$ is closed under matrix addition” is false. For example, if ${A}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},$ then\n${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ each contain a row consisting only of zeros, so they are not invertible. However,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis invertible. So, $S$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement “$S$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is true. Indeed, if $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix that is not invertible then $det(A)=0$ and therefore for all $\\alpha \\in R$ \n\n$$\ndet(\\alpha A)={\\alpha }^{2}\\cdot det(A)={\\alpha }^{2}\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $S$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$S$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is false, while statement “$S$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is true. $S$ is a *not* subspace because it's not closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$S$ is closed under scalar multiplication”; “$S$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378355 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9334923c-62ff-50b8-adbe-4ed7ab4703c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453218} {:answer/id #uuid "ad2db7a3-d7e9-5c61-9a1a-c8ccad0f7961" :answer/type {:db/