53222} :answer-field/id #uuid "a00a0fe6-f9a7-5605-ad3a-48fa5eb0728e" :answer-field/key "$B$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454361} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ebc8a07b-3466-5170-9f69-0e8c3685f3c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453224} {:answer/id #uuid "1f40564c-9555-5959-bca0-0f63995ff413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f40564c-9555-5959-bca0-0f63995ff413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453225} :answer-field/id #uuid "affc55ed-ee15-5b9d-b758-210c15c8f69b" :answer-field/key "$B$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ff663474-9982-50d0-b983-22c1b4e4d38b" :question/math-academy-id "q-107144" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $B={f\\in C[0,1]\\,|\\,\\,f(x)\\le 1\\,\\,∀x\\in [0,1]}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$B$ is closed under function addition” is false. For example, if  $f(x)=g(x)=1$ for all $x\\in [0,1]$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(x) & =f(x)+g(x) \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2 \\\\  & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in [0,1].$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement “$B$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. Let, for example,  $f(x)=1$ for all $x\\in [0,1]$ and take and $k=2,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(x) & =2f(x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2 \\\\  & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in [0,1].$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$B$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$” is false, while statement “$B$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$” is true. $B$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$B$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9c8b6f7-a765-51f0-bdc1-0e20609fa1e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453226} {:answer/id #uuid "75058ef8-65b5-5339-9bcb-1c1175a9c585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9c8b6f7-a765-51f0-bdc1-0e20609fa1e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453226} :answer-field/id #uuid "603a8296-6812-5aa0-acca-2e58013b4290" :answer-field/key "$K$ is closed under function addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454363} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aea5044e-ffdb-5981-9a0d-1e77af7bb0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453228} {:answer/id #uuid "5e12f28f-5d7e-5ae4-9e88-d666b37d25f5" :answer/type {: