 :answer-field/id #uuid "88425d2a-b4ad-54eb-89a3-3a3b986d9505" :answer-field/key "$K$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ecd1a414-f091-5cfd-86f0-d0c82f6d9564" :question/math-academy-id "q-107147" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $K$ containing all nonconstant functions.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n*Hint: $f$ is a constant function if $f(x)=\\text{constant}$ for all $x\\in [0,1].$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$K$ is closed under function addition” is false. For example, the functions $f(x)=x+2$ and $f(x)=-x-1$ are in $K$, however\n\n$$\n(f+g)(x)=1\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in [0,1]$ and hence $f+g$ is a constant function. \nSo, $K$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement “$K$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. For example, the product of the scalar zero by any function is the constant function zero. So, $K$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$K$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$” is false, while statement “$K$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$” is true. $K$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$K$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124614 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66b24a98-c641-5e08-8bec-30f221d1bb22" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Stochastic Vectors and Stochastic Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "490995ed-ac99-5768-ad40-5b0e11f10a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471033} {:answer/id #uuid "484cb763-07fa-5ad2-a411-8df07f51dab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "490995ed-ac99-5768-ad40-5b0e11f10a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471033} :answer-field/id #uuid "42e6465e-3deb-5f06-abdf-59086e80b9f5" :answer-field/key "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 1.1 & 0.8\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472022} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e74dd853-f834-5489-9ab6-2207e01c886a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471035} {:answer/id #uuid "41a85770-ab01-5832-833b-ff27a5be8436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41a85770-ab01-5832-833b-ff27a5be8436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471036} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b48cb6c-8acd-5de5-896e-2355e9e0e35d" :answer-field/key "$V=\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.9 & 0.8\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472023} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2269aad-57fb-5cbb-ab49-87e39a9ac7cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471037} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f0420b-4735-51ba-ba16-ed5ea138cc6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0f0420b-4735-51ba-ba16-ed5ea138cc6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471038} :answer-field/id #uuid "1807e1b7-7969-53ae-b85d-f2a54b4c14bf" :answer-field/key "$W=\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & 0 & 0.5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0.5 & 0 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "90365b47-9514-5b9b-bb0b-216780f54607" :question/math-academy-id "q-135487" :question/problem "Which of the following are stochastic matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$ A matrix is stochastic if all its columns are stochastic vectors.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices in turn.\n\n- Matrix $U$ is *not* a stochastic matrix since its first column is not a stochastic vector (it contains negative entries): \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 1.1 & 0.8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Matrix $V$ is a stochastic matrix. Indeed, each column is a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries are nonnegative and add up to one): \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.9 & 0.8\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\begin{aligned}0.1+0.9=1 \\\\ 0.2+0.8=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Matrix $W$ is a stochastic matrix. Indeed, each column is a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries are non-negative and add up to one): \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & 0 & 0.5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0.5 & 0 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\begin{aligned}0.5+0+0.5=1 \\\\ 0+1+0=1 \\\\ 0.5+0+0.5=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$V$ and $W$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378850 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9adda67-6a0c-5ed4-88d6-f2c76756703b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453478} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2f32a5-a444-594a-bc7b-ca880ea1cd72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e2f32a5-a444-594a-bc7b-ca880ea1cd72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453479} :answer-field/id #uuid "15835f11-1852-5f58-8f9c-38beabfab106" :answer-field/key "$A$ contains none of its boundary points." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454489} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9fc8eb5-59a6-579e-81ba-64fd489210be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453480} {:answer/id #uuid "af6822f2-5255-5beb-841a-3c878f5590b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9fc8eb5-59a6-579e-81ba-64fd489210be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453480} :answer-field/id #uuid "22ca5593-aa89-50a4-ac84-0aa89a5388d2" :answer-field/key "$A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454490} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75722349-8129-514e-85ed-4febc75783fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453482} {:answer/id #uuid "670ceb03-fec6-5ece-97e4-9b966c32f487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "670ceb03-fec6-5ece-97e4-9b966c32f487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453483} :answer-field/id #uuid "29a80115-d74f-5e30-affe-dd0cd38775ee" :answer-field/key "$\\text{int}\\,A=A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454491}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7cfd8147-c3e0-5cab-9b14-cee4034ac307" :question/math-academy-id "q-161623" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/c2/c2b4e3d11f16920ce24a279289808d3f5dc4e68563525f1417c8767a5446b461.png)\n\n \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement “$A$ contains none of its boundary points” is true, while statement “$A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points” is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement $\\text{int}\\,A=A$ is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ contains none of its boundary points”; $\\text{int}\\,A=A$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16604ddb-69ca-5ace-9dbf-0383a82ea98e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471113} {:answer/id #uuid "ed093c42-08ca-5342-9c3d-5d707ac0618a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16604ddb-69ca-5ace-9dbf-0383a82ea98e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471113} :answer-field/id #uuid "271f6907-9f07-58b0-b69e-9138291c3f29" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,0<x<2,\\\\\\,0<y<x\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472062} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8be1298c-3ffd-5e63-bdaf-4b61ccf3b37b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471115} {:answer/id #uuid "257b2998-d432-57cf-9773-e11354e3ef90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "257b2998-d432-57cf-9773-e11354e3ef90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471116} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c83fa2d-fc72-5a50-960b-e7f3fe4261ae" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472063} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae39a58d-0d80-5e95-a397-418e9ba63826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471117} {:answer/id #uuid "974db8f3-030a-560c-ab7c-a6b736fbe846" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "974db8f3-030a-560c-ab7c-a6b736fbe846" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471118} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b5293d9-c7c0-526b-9f08-83692bebc37d" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472064}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28c149d9-63e5-5d01-abf9-5e8569624b8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161639" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$; $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378864 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7519ae6-6283-5e9b-a86d-15f672cad5d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471119} {:answer/id #uuid "18729287-882a-5576-aa4a-14fe49a63438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18729287-882a-5576-aa4a-14fe49a63438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471120} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6c5d9db-d0d7-59d7-a450-9db137467fd8" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }0<x<3,\\\\\\,0<y<6-2x\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472065} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "734986cb-f797-5efd-8757-8769d869f4d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471121} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7892cb-fc1c-5d4d-b659-5a1cd819479f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d7892cb-fc1c-5d4d-b659-5a1cd819479f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471122} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c231af6-4c3a-595b-b7f7-a6f8e18ec0c9" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }1<x<4,\\\\\\,x<y<{x}^{2}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472066} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ff0b204-8f86-56a6-929a-934210b283ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471123} {:answer/id #uuid "5a900764-35ba-5f4f-b5a5-cd518fee058c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ff0b204-8f86-56a6-929a-934210b283ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471123} :answer-field/id #uuid "a90ac0c3-b368-5769-b866-780b1af534a5" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }-1\\le x\\le 1,\\\\\\,0\\le {y}^{2}\\le 5\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be4d8952-950b-5fb0-a574-0337f64e1d84" :question/math-academy-id "q-161648" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }0<x<3,\\\\\\,0<y<6-2x\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$; $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }1<x<4,\\\\\\,x<y<{x}^{2}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f311c265-2bb0-5ad1-815d-44417f1e31a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471125} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffdf529-09c7-5cab-a876-7f9b20669834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ffdf529-09c7-5cab-a876-7f9b20669834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471126} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8b400c0-9b95-56f2-8848-67709fb87921" :answer-field/key "$\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472068} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95b0b167-a547-50ff-8123-620fe621a81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471127} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c742b0-471f-59d1-924e-69676e078128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95b0b167-a547-50ff-8123-620fe621a81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471127} :answer-field/id #uuid "af3cb4bf-3026-5dbf-bb69-ac0bfdbd1d57" :answer-field/key "$A⊂\\text{int}A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472069} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0799b728-a09d-5e7c-a241-f50801a2ea50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471129} {:answer/id #uuid "5f8c5826-4aff-5dff-9a12-8d4de0ce361f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f8c5826-4aff-5dff-9a12-8d4de0ce361f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471130} :answer-field/id #uuid "26da464c-3c67-5b3b-808a-3b3403f4ed69" :answer-field/key "$A-\\text{int}A=∂A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6e963f0b-a2c7-5ae0-844a-f3e405d79aa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161649" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x\\ge {y}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88f35519cf1aa01bcc9e4fb91b24c2bc2a1a823867ec2670563b0b45f2643a0a.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/64/649c33f1738a35f3d298038bd2cf05d3b435424a4efbbb1e6143cf0d56b2bfd6.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A$ is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A.$\n\n- Statement $A⊂\\text{int}A$ is false. In this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points, so we must have $A⊈\\text{int}A.$\n\n- Statement $A-\\text{int}A=∂A$ is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $A-\\text{int}A=∂A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A$; $A-\\text{int}A=∂A$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eda1965-d655-5550-9bb5-13e7a9c1b406" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statements Expressed Using Symbols"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f435800-2b81-5947-90ad-4a74eb1dee76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471173} {:answer/id #uuid "6727caa3-b8d4-5efd-ad79-327dfcf9a99b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f435800-2b81-5947-90ad-4a74eb1dee76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471173} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8a97d97-a433-557a-b652-db4fb249f128" :answer-field/key "$P:(-2)\\cdot 3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472092} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da3dfff1-b7cd-50d8-96d9-be0504b46dfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471175} {:answer/id #uuid "2a0fa50e-4733-5f26-87e6-0a746393b628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a0fa50e-4733-5f26-87e6-0a746393b628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471176} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbc0c852-246a-5a48-8f9d-dc39d0951ae6" :answer-field/key "$Q:5>3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472093} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0540e3ae-15bc-5c25-96ce-77d4312aef86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471177} {:answer/id #uuid "0474c37a-87c9-5fe3-9dae-73199fcc1276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0474c37a-87c9-5fe3-9dae-73199fcc1276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471178} :answer-field/id #uuid "26bfe548-4be8-50f0-b988-9ed0c686fec9" :answer-field/key "$R:7\\in N$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66e732f7-06d5-591e-98a5-b6812f6bf5f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-174419" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\n- $Q$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because $5$ is larger than  $3.$\n\n- $R$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because $7$ is a natural number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q$ and $R$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379134 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4d607d8-d309-5ca9-83bc-740b4c36bade" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471191} {:answer/id #uuid "325fb8bb-d47f-5880-a8b1-b79555ac108d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "325fb8bb-d47f-5880-a8b1-b79555ac108d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471192} :answer-field/id #uuid "42d12dc6-b94a-52d8-8494-2498d1c73f28" :answer-field/key "$P({R,e})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472101} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53559d5d-159d-5fdc-bd9d-4e94bdf5ac8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471193} {:answer/id #uuid "d6e30a64-f23f-5094-890c-8e7f4d8a8222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53559d5d-159d-5fdc-bd9d-4e94bdf5ac8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471193} :answer-field/id #uuid "b856be72-7e15-5ad6-945e-6975defb3028" :answer-field/key "$P({x\\in R∣\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b52a727-ad5e-5373-9c5a-a0274dde1602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471195} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8607f7-f14a-5008-becc-2bb0c03d4f5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc8607f7-f14a-5008-becc-2bb0c03d4f5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471196} :answer-field/id #uuid "5def3004-16f9-5b6c-af86-0253fe70b521" :answer-field/key "$P({(-1)^{n}∣n\\in Z})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c162f27f-023e-512b-91b9-54632834b487" :question/math-academy-id "q-182238" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are finite?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The power set of a finite set is finite, while the power set of an infinite set is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Set $P({R,e})$ is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\nP({R,e})={∅,\\,{R},\\,{e},\\,{R,e}}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $4.$\n\n- Set $P({x\\in R∣\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0})$ is infinite since the underlying set ${x\\in R∣\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0}$  is infinite.\n\n- Set $P({(-1)^{n}∣n\\in Z})$ is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\n{(-1)^{n}∣n\\in Z}={-1,1},\n$$\n\nand, as a result, \n\n$$\nP({(-1)^{n}∣n\\in Z})=P({-1,1})={∅,\\,{-1},\\,{1},\\,{-1,1}}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P({R,e})$; $P({(-1)^{n}∣n\\in Z})$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aab99129-4a35-5556-a306-b270209eb006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471197} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf24b5c-acad-501b-ba57-b7184be25122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdf24b5c-acad-501b-ba57-b7184be25122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471198} :answer-field/id #uuid "6763cbff-5062-54e7-8246-c7e4594fed34" :answer-field/key "$P({Z,t,n})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aef9dd66-34ea-5dbf-a0dd-8474aee33837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471199} {:answer/id #uuid "fdd0b854-f3ec-55e0-ab08-b2d4550ee97e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aef9dd66-34ea-5dbf-a0dd-8474aee33837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471199} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5e493a5-5150-5cd4-919d-2373e95ae21f" :answer-field/key "$P(Z)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f0bb31f-6825-5c25-8cf0-baac756459f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471201} {:answer/id #uuid "fd50a221-4939-518b-9637-343788a92231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f0bb31f-6825-5c25-8cf0-baac756459f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471201} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8f2aeba-3fe6-5e39-aeca-5cc3601e1920" :answer-field/key "$P({{2}^{n}∣n\\in Z})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d277777-ae06-5b12-9091-65c43e7bf489" :question/math-academy-id "q-182241" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are finite?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The power set of a finite set is finite, while the power set of an infinite set is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Set $P({Z,t,n})$ is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\nP({Z,t,n})={∅,\\,{Z},\\,{t},\\,{n},\\,{Z,t},{Z,n},\\,{t,n},\\,{Z,t,n}}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $8.$\n\n- Set $P(Z)$ is infinite since the underlying set $Z$ is infinite.\n\n- Set $P({{2}^{n}∣n\\in Z})$ is infinite since the underlying set ${{2}^{n}∣n\\in Z}$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P({Z,t,n})$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d56b033-a2c8-57c7-adde-e574d726ec78" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting Symbolic Conditional Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "103ba745-89da-572a-8645-0e48e298eb69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453628} {:answer/id #uuid "6db316e3-11cf-581e-aba4-72198d752449" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "103ba745-89da-572a-8645-0e48e298eb69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453628} :answer-field/id #uuid "08fbb3c2-9e09-5166-81cf-b13e5f40f715" :answer-field/key "$¬P⇒Q≡P∨¬Q$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454564} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8908055-e767-5cc9-8603-c9755f6acf08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453630} {:answer/id #uuid "2dee54e9-a7cf-5ff7-8cb7-66dd7d69200c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8908055-e767-5cc9-8603-c9755f6acf08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453630} :answer-field/id #uuid "605e62e8-9662-50d1-bfd8-1829ceb621ed" :answer-field/key "$¬(¬P⇒Q)≡¬P∧Q$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454565} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7adbcc1-3421-5d01-aa06-a9b6e0ef1051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453632} {:answer/id #uuid "502be7d4-5665-556d-b837-f469b7e58366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "502be7d4-5665-556d-b837-f469b7e58366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453633} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3efa2ca-31f9-5aba-80a2-9f4d61b15725" :answer-field/key "$¬(¬P⇒Q)≡¬P∧¬Q$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b9dc8cb9-65d8-59f4-a25c-a9f9b514997d" :question/math-academy-id "q-182505" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements:\n\n- Statement $¬P⇒Q≡P∨¬Q$ is false. Indeed, $¬P⇒Q$ is logically equivalent to the disjunction $¬(¬P)∨Q,$ which in turn is equivalent to $P∨Q.$\n\n- Statement $¬(¬P⇒Q)≡¬P∧Q$ is false, while statement $¬(¬P⇒Q)≡¬P∧¬Q$ is true. From part $¬P⇒Q≡P∨¬Q$, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$$\n¬P⇒Q≡P∨Q\n$$\n\nBy negating this statement, we get\n\n$$\n¬(¬P⇒Q)≡¬(P∨Q).\n$$\n\nDistributing the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law, we have\n\n$$\n¬(P∨Q)≡¬P∧¬Q.\n$$\n\nSo, $¬(¬P⇒Q)$ is equivalent to $¬P∧¬Q.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $¬(¬P⇒Q)≡¬P∧¬Q$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5c38a40-b0ad-50a0-b1fd-3ca0ed423d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471221} {:answer/id #uuid "b4471eda-3004-561c-b183-28b096dbfdb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5c38a40-b0ad-50a0-b1fd-3ca0ed423d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471221} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb1c9fc7-d87b-54a3-a66e-faa888700146" :answer-field/key "If $4\\in {2,4,8},$ then $8$ is even." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3ed57af-e278-5ede-a755-783ce9ed8c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471223} {:answer/id #uuid "761ff025-d2e6-53d2-985e-4816ac004c2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "761ff025-d2e6-53d2-985e-4816ac004c2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471224} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc9e2ea8-4854-5a7a-8552-15585b54efc9" :answer-field/key "If $4\\notin {2,4,8},$ then $8$ is not even." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f4f384a-3166-5f09-b657-4055cb82802e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471225} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc1fc9d-3e88-590e-be39-355512cb0a6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f4f384a-3166-5f09-b657-4055cb82802e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471225} :answer-field/id #uuid "c34ffd8a-bcff-52d9-a081-61d20b6aec70" :answer-field/key "If $8$ is not even, then $4\\notin {2,4,8}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472118}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d0274f7-9e96-5c91-af2a-50bf61bf0ba6" :question/math-academy-id "q-183341" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** $8$ is even **then** $4\\in {2,4,8}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement “If $4\\in {2,4,8},$ then $8$ is even” is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement “If $4\\notin {2,4,8},$ then $8$ is not even” is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement “If $8$ is not even, then $4\\notin {2,4,8}.$” is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If $4\\notin {2,4,8},$ then $8$ is not even” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f6920b1-2a94-5a47-840f-c823c9f70e36" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing General Solutions of First-Order Linear Systems of ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bbc9cee-6d9f-53b6-a3f9-35050e0dd0fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471383} {:answer/id #uuid "4f002261-81ab-55ff-af9f-9a2b2a621724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f002261-81ab-55ff-af9f-9a2b2a621724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471384} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3a28f8d-5383-5eca-ab07-4ecdbad60269" :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}(t)-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472197} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26c62176-2c72-5180-a83a-f3021cb5c0a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471385} {:answer/id #uuid "059fa7d6-c973-5f8c-b14c-0bf94b31437b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "059fa7d6-c973-5f8c-b14c-0bf94b31437b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471386} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d943dfd-579b-532f-b5c1-a67bf7f7b2f3" :answer-field/key "$-7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472198} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64b0de36-67f4-5fbd-bc5c-7e6fbd2cc1eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471387} {:answer/id #uuid "899f8325-7fc0-5e7f-aed3-fc93ba710d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64b0de36-67f4-5fbd-bc5c-7e6fbd2cc1eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471387} :answer-field/id #uuid "f68de2b5-cce3-546e-85e3-13db4ede6900" :answer-field/key "$2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec98e74e-e68c-5045-a599-d3ec1260eaf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-330299" :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)+f(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${x}_{h}(t)$ satisfies a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution to an inhomogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ then ${x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is also a solution to the same inhomogeneous system.\n\nAdditonally, the *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t),…,{x}_{k}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then any linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)+⋯+{c}_{k}{x}_{k}(t)\n$$\n\nwith ${c}_{1},{c}_{2},…,{c}_{k}\\in R$ is also a solution of the same homogeneous system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expression.\n\n- Option ${x}_{1}(t)-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=1\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{{x}_{1}(t)-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option $-7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=-7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{-7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\n- Option $2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$ might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that $2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $2$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${x}_{1}(t)-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$; $-7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f6920b1-2a94-5a47-840f-c823c9f70e36" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing General Solutions of First-Order Linear Systems of ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2a88b9c-22ee-5b00-af09-d1cdae976ad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471389} {:answer/id #uuid "699c223a-b0f1-5ab1-9742-cc8cc24e7610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2a88b9c-22ee-5b00-af09-d1cdae976ad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471389} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fe7b73e-c8d1-5806-97dd-83443a307c30" :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472200} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f77fbd2-8e41-54f7-8dab-495bfe9057db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471391} {:answer/id #uuid "b928d8c6-5415-580d-a8fc-bfe309b7a281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f77fbd2-8e41-54f7-8dab-495bfe9057db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471391} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc36a6ef-b56b-5871-97f4-e7173861f357" :answer-field/key "$-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{p}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472201} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5134166f-f275-568c-8bbb-42b5f7da138d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471393} {:answer/id #uuid "37b63443-245b-500c-9c9b-3ed20a0c4b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37b63443-245b-500c-9c9b-3ed20a0c4b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471394} :answer-field/id #uuid "07370987-e91d-5a14-9c0b-88a34bdf1ab6" :answer-field/key "$-6\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+9\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "028e3468-5c29-5e67-a28b-97b2d534ac0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-330306" :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)+f(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${x}_{h}(t)$ satisfies a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution to an inhomogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ then ${x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is also a solution to the same inhomogeneous system.\n\nAdditonally, the *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t),…,{x}_{k}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then any linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)+⋯+{c}_{k}{x}_{k}(t)\n$$\n\nwith ${c}_{1},{c}_{2},…,{c}_{k}\\in R$ is also a solution of the same homogeneous system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expression.\n\n- Option ${x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$ might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that ${x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $2$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\n- Option $-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{p}(t)$ might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that $-5\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $-1$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\n- Option $-6\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+9\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Indeed, notice that the linear combination \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)=-6\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+9\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ according to the linearity principle. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{-6\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+9\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)}_{{x}_{h}(t)}+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nis a solution to our inhomogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-6\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+9\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379604 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12a9f9cf-06f6-51b8-ba41-a8b6300a5c2b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Ordinary and Singular Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c540cb1b-69f7-5f99-bad5-ce4fb3967ef8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471435} {:answer/id #uuid "53b186d2-81f0-5610-928c-351f854cf04f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53b186d2-81f0-5610-928c-351f854cf04f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471436} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5fd9f56-7c1c-5e45-b553-b8266c8209ea" :answer-field/key "$x=-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472223} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8441d8c-043c-5a17-9a39-6a5dea8a1934" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471437} {:answer/id #uuid "59044e28-9bad-5f71-afa3-7e02f334e2e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59044e28-9bad-5f71-afa3-7e02f334e2e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471438} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7bf0c61-d4ff-567d-8e2b-5981962d2d56" :answer-field/key "$x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c7c0fbf-2b18-5fad-bedf-cab28bfd9c60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471439} {:answer/id #uuid "c1eb06ad-9786-5477-89a2-338126df89db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c7c0fbf-2b18-5fad-bedf-cab28bfd9c60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471439} :answer-field/id #uuid "94df1425-9126-5127-93c1-dfb7144e6014" :answer-field/key "$x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472225}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff653b13-8b67-5277-ad4c-9f98277f418a" :question/math-academy-id "q-342282" :question/problem "$$\nx(x+3){y}^{″}+(x-2){y}^{′}+4y=0\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a **singular** point of the differential equation above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The point $x=a$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nif both coefficients $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, $x=a$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $x(x+3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(x+3){y}^{″}+(x-2){y}^{′}+4y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{x-2}{x(x+3)}{y}^{′}+\\frac{4}{x(x+3)}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{x-2}{x(x+3)}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{4}{x(x+3)}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check the analyticity of these functions at the given points.\n\n- *Neither* function is analytic about $x=-3,$ since both denominators at $x=-3$ equal zero. So, $x=-3$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\n- *Neither* function is analytic about $x=0,$ since both denominators at $x=0$ equal zero. So, $x=0$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\n- *Both* functions are analytic about $x=2.$ So, $x=2$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-3$; $x=0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e7d1368-06ee-5135-b9f4-d3d4d2756b32" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regular and Irregular Singular Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5772d6f-b4c4-5b0f-a341-7bcce7c53ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471441} {:answer/id #uuid "72f28384-9464-531f-83ec-b7d7d44da974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5772d6f-b4c4-5b0f-a341-7bcce7c53ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471441} :answer-field/id #uuid "3de9898a-65aa-5f5c-a471-68d4884d2a25" :answer-field/key "The functions $P(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x+3}$ are analytic about $x=-3.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472226} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f34e0f7-5c36-57be-8be0-72cd026a3c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471443} {:answer/id #uuid "545a20a3-dc0a-54e0-a437-92e4bb0d8db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f34e0f7-5c36-57be-8be0-72cd026a3c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471443} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e5ae857-3730-5c76-9614-b81b46af3e2a" :answer-field/key "The functions $(x+3)P(x)$ and $(x+3)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=-3.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472227} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "331a7444-e6ed-5b95-9c85-51c56d8adc44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471445} {:answer/id #uuid "0dd04662-64d9-59d1-be58-90ecddce155e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0dd04662-64d9-59d1-be58-90ecddce155e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471446} :answer-field/id #uuid "377eb8bf-59f3-5a09-928e-03ed7443b513" :answer-field/key "The point $x=-3$ is an **irregular** singular point of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39331851-2b44-5819-96f4-7d54c8cd9bd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-342366" :question/problem "$$\n(x+3){y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{2}}{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A singular point $a$ of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nis regular if both $(x-a)P(x)$ and $(x-a)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, the singular point is irregular.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $(x+3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3){y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{2}}{y}^{′}+y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{x+3}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check each statement in turn.\n\n- Since the denominators of both $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ vanish at $x=-3,$ they are *not* analytic about $x=-3.$ So, statement “The functions $P(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x+3}$ are analytic about $x=-3.$” is false.\n\n- The function\n\n$$\n(x+3)P(x)=(x+3)\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{2}}\n$$\n\n is *not* analytic about $x=-3$ since its denominator vanishes at $x=-3.$ Therefore, statement “The functions $(x+3)P(x)$ and $(x+3)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=-3.$” is false.\n\n- Since statement “The functions $P(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x+3}$ are analytic about $x=-3.$” is false, $x=-3$ is a singular point. Also, since statement “The functions $(x+3)P(x)$ and $(x+3)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=-3.$” is false, it follows that $x=-3$ is an **irregular** singular point. Thus, statement “The point $x=-3$ is an **irregular** singular point of the differential equation” is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The point $x=-3$ is an **irregular** singular point of the differential equation” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379766 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5582e4fd-2c1b-5d7e-8c00-e97e06814dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471447} {:answer/id #uuid "a3eb097d-ca23-5819-ac10-dc59c55d7b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3eb097d-ca23-5819-ac10-dc59c55d7b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471448} :answer-field/id #uuid "d03efb8d-a67e-5194-9397-44b10a9fe206" :answer-field/key "$c=-1$ gives a line" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472229} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "398cb7dd-8121-5f92-b1f8-3cb5dfa077bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471449} {:answer/id #uuid "835ea12a-0dec-59ad-8c9d-1e2c535804ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "398cb7dd-8121-5f92-b1f8-3cb5dfa077bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471449} :answer-field/id #uuid "671dd875-2b17-5bf5-8cd4-e539f182cfa9" :answer-field/key "$c=0$ gives the axes $x=0$ and $y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472230} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c761f2b5-ba81-5508-8846-69bc0e2a0948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471451} {:answer/id #uuid "e051646c-5725-58cc-bba2-10290a7faee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c761f2b5-ba81-5508-8846-69bc0e2a0948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471451} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac6ae07c-0a83-5d77-ab7d-cfed78b60de1" :answer-field/key "$c=2$ gives a parabola" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472231}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "036af2f8-8d3f-5a9f-9714-c21bb558dc15" :question/math-academy-id "q-35538" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=4x-3y-1$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3y-1 & =c \\\\ 4x-3y-(c+1) & =0 \\\\ y & =\\frac{4}{3}x-\\frac{c+1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=-1$ then the level curve is $y=\\frac{4}{3}x,$ which is a line.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=\\frac{4}{3}x-\\frac{1}{3},$ which is a line different to the axes $x=0$ and $y=0.$\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is $y=\\frac{4}{3}x-1,$ which is not a parabola.\n\nSo, only statement “$c=-1$ gives a line” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d046747a-b317-586d-8d55-5c90d106b70d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471459} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ae2f16-5c4b-5f1c-bc31-c6238c4fb198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d046747a-b317-586d-8d55-5c90d106b70d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471459} :answer-field/id #uuid "e01cb9ca-cfef-5a04-b8e8-faaa3c67d474" :answer-field/key "$c=0$ gives a circle" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c5c8627-87dd-5f0d-836a-c310a9c4ed71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471461} {:answer/id #uuid "6bf51cce-838b-5461-8589-29027a79ad48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c5c8627-87dd-5f0d-836a-c310a9c4ed71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471461} :answer-field/id #uuid "9af77a4f-7777-5db4-b47d-afe23125eeb7" :answer-field/key "$c=1$ gives a hyperbola" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472236} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5aadc0f6-aa90-5bee-94bc-57244da99e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471463} {:answer/id #uuid "46907805-5ba1-518e-903b-c1d4d29ff9d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46907805-5ba1-518e-903b-c1d4d29ff9d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471464} :answer-field/id #uuid "af943ca9-e995-586e-81d8-b5176e4f024d" :answer-field/key "$c=2$ gives a parabola" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3aaf864-2fae-5bdc-a851-6e2a3303364c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71398" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2y}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2y} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+2y & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is not a circle.\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is $y=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is not a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is $y=2-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is a parabola.\n\nSo, only statement “$c=2$ gives a parabola” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49cf872d-689f-5e2e-9332-695ac6faa1d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471483} {:answer/id #uuid "a0b69705-0fc5-56cf-9a35-6c357cb97eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0b69705-0fc5-56cf-9a35-6c357cb97eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471484} :answer-field/id #uuid "68f67652-3fb0-559a-89e4-313feeaf26f0" :answer-field/key "$[-2,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472247} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54aa25bf-5940-59e0-a6aa-ae17ece3e229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471485} {:answer/id #uuid "72bc58dc-bdb3-5d78-b56d-a3ff427f2c41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72bc58dc-bdb3-5d78-b56d-a3ff427f2c41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471486} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c956b2c-afaf-5232-8dd1-6441df297688" :answer-field/key "$[3,9]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472248} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dc3df3f-0a2f-58b6-8cc0-dd5b0c759bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471487} {:answer/id #uuid "694f2513-41e1-5b51-8e18-a72cf04d9069" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dc3df3f-0a2f-58b6-8cc0-dd5b0c759bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471487} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4377199-a8d0-5db1-a161-0f59b2917c34" :answer-field/key "$[-1,1)\\cup (3,4]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d4218ace-9c46-5876-8096-9bc751d57412" :question/math-academy-id "q-71793" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[-2,2]$ and $[3,9]$ are closed because:\n\n- The boundary points of $[-2,2]$ are $-2$, and $2.$ Both of them lie in the set.\n\n- The boundary points of $[3,9]$ are $3$, and $9.$ Both of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other set is not closed because $[-1,1)\\cup (3,4]$ has a boundary point $1$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $[-2,2]$; $[3,9]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a89a159-240f-5646-9d9d-07e5c88ba649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471489} {:answer/id #uuid "3d1f9b96-8b9d-594b-8ea8-d5a1eaad1bcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a89a159-240f-5646-9d9d-07e5c88ba649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471489} :answer-field/id #uuid "0833ee3c-9acf-5