71795" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[0,2]\\cup [6,7]$ is closed. It consists of two parts, where the boundary points are $0,2,6,$ and $7.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not closed because:\n\n- $(-3,1)$ has a boundary point $1$, which does not lie in the set.\n\n- $(-1,3)\\cup (4,7]$ has a boundary point $3$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $[0,2]\\cup [6,7]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ed61332-13c7-5cfe-bd7d-b74b4269a49f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471495} {:answer/id #uuid "62d38bc3-1662-5473-abf7-d55153533159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ed61332-13c7-5cfe-bd7d-b74b4269a49f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471495} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3655b78-dca0-5c5f-a7ea-0a3af751b3aa" :answer-field/key "$(6,10]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472253} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4d94e16-9fb4-