ly of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[2,5]$ and $[0,1]\\cup [3,4]$ are closed because:\n\n- The boundary points of $[2,5]$ are $2$ and $5.$ Both of them lie in the set.\n\n- The boundary points of $[0,1]\\cup [3,4]$ are $0,1,3,$ and $4.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other set is not closed because $(6,10]$ has a boundary point $6$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $[2,5]$; $[0,1]\\cup [3,4]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4d0a02e-b9a7-5533-ba1a-2f80acfdd774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471501} {:answer/id #uuid "3634b9a6-d22a-5361-aa5e-75a49f2a1180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4d0a02e-b9a7-5533-ba1a-2f80acfdd774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471501} :answer-field/id #uuid "6abbef18-93ea-56dd-b268-7018d23ddfa8" :answer-field/key "$(-2,1]\\cup [3,9)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472256} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f8f10a7-0a63-5ee4-bf6e-1ee054e2c178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471503} {:answer/id #uuid "2f6d0c4f-4b1a-5d9e-9cdc-49d1f07cf01e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f8f10a7-0a63-5ee4-bf6e-1ee054e2c178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471503} :answer-field/id #uuid "f04b2162-9644-5318-a58f-b073768907c2" :answer-field/key "$[4,6)\\cup (9,11)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472257} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da2799fe-1894-5db5-bc3f-8d59a60ca339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471505} {:answer/id #uuid "97dfe6de-be4b-5960-b11e-8aa543d47602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97dfe6de-be4b-5960-b11e-8aa543d47602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471506} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6f3acd4-15de-55a8-9779-2caa89a1cd1c" :answer-field/key "$(-1,4)\\cup (6,7)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472258}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0cdf362-49b4-5e81-91f4-944c2a137d99" :question/math-academy-id "q-71801" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-1,4)\\cup (6,7)$ is open. It consists of two parts, where the boundary points are $-1$, $4$, $6$, and $7.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $(-2,1]\\cup [3,9)$ has four boundary points $-2$, $1$, $3$, and $9$, and the points $1$ and $3$ lie in the set.\n\n- $[4,6)\\cup (9,11)$ has four boundary points $4$, $6$, $9$, and $11$, and the point $4$ lies in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $(-1,4)\\cup (6,7)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29610715-333d-5e0c-9328-eec1d45f56ed" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Limits Along Different Paths for Multivariable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87ce1ae9-57eb-59cd-8da4-c1a0d3076afc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453952} {:answer/id #uuid "ebff1072-dded-550a-b750-8d400dcf93f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87ce1ae9-57eb-59cd-8da4-c1a0d3076afc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453952} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e09413b-af06-58f6-88c6-125426ab31d4" :answer-field/key "The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454726} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "776c0c2e-2277-507d-b18d-ed1e84b4ed82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453954} {:answer/id #uuid "7b3dfc88-d38f-581f-9c20-80e64cbb04cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b3dfc88-d38f-581f-9c20-80e64cbb04cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453955} :answer-field/id #uuid "27ee9fb1-8544-5a36-b32c-707df9287960" :answer-field/key "The limit evaluates to $1$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454727} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36ca50ed-9faf-5c4a-bf22-4d644e34ef62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453956} {:answer/id #uuid "161c0d73-cc78-5569-9199-8fc986254f2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36ca50ed-9faf-5c4a-bf22-4d644e34ef62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453956} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b63f72f-ca55-514b-bc37-6bef9f319ce0" :answer-field/key "The limit exists and is equal to $1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb1f3bd1-4155-5e86-902f-cd91483f7d31" :question/math-academy-id "q-74963" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}=\\frac{{0}^{2}}{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement “The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=x$” is false. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+(x)^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The limit evaluates to $1$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$” is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{2}}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{({x}^{2})}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{x}^{4}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+0} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The limit exists and is equal to $1$” is false. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}=\\text{DNE}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e815afe7-e4a5-5591-9f0e-2bf26f3075b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471669} {:answer/id #uuid "d75542aa-7263-5d8d-b51a-d9df54c992a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e815afe7-e4a5-5591-9f0e-2bf26f3075b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471669} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef7dcfed-0835-5f2a-a484-e51cc3784d92" :answer-field/key "$¬R∧(Q∧¬R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472340} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19efdde4-e8a8-57ef-b8cd-2e6daeb6231a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471671} {:answer/id #uuid "541c39ec-dfcb-5f4e-b641-2498e75c6b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "541c39ec-dfcb-5f4e-b641-2498e75c6b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471672} :answer-field/id #uuid "dadb9685-5531-5d90-9da3-34529ac942d4" :answer-field/key "$Q∧(¬R∨Q)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472341} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5f9bcaf-a69c-5760-9bb5-b9f9e9c51c62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471673} {:answer/id #uuid "faf64540-f9e0-59af-8fe6-792306c1dc9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "faf64540-f9e0-59af-8fe6-792306c1dc9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471674} :answer-field/id #uuid "33e6f530-6801-54f7-b77e-828d18b79824" :answer-field/key "$(¬R∨Q)∧Q$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f1b738de-914d-5dd9-b0ba-d383cdcec6e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-81718" :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $Q?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The law that conjunction absorbs disjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nQ∧(Q∨¬R)≡Q.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement $¬R∧(Q∧¬R)$ is *not* logically equivalent to $Q.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement $Q∧(¬R∨Q)$ is logically equivalent to $Q.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q∧(¬R∨Q) & ≡Q∧(Q∨¬R) \\\\  & ≡Q.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement $(¬R∨Q)∧Q$ is logically equivalent to $Q.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(¬R∨Q)∧Q & ≡Q∧(Q∨¬R) \\\\  & ≡Q.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $Q∧(¬R∨Q)$; $(¬R∨Q)∧Q$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d4ea352-2a82-5ff5-8c08-b7f9a09929e6" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Disjunction Absorbs Conjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fdf284e-9487-5165-8099-9a3790efb82e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471675} {:answer/id #uuid "bf83dccc-5552-5b53-84c0-f6a1db81fd77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf83dccc-5552-5b53-84c0-f6a1db81fd77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471676} :answer-field/id #uuid "186c50d7-c389-5340-b8c1-e4f73539aa4e" :answer-field/key "$P∨(Q∧P)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472343} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fead6e3-8bf7-5704-bad1-5890cb3e5698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471677} {:answer/id #uuid "6053ef7d-3571-55dc-8b54-94ba163c0aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6053ef7d-3571-55dc-8b54-94ba163c0aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471678} :answer-field/id #uuid "add17c71-ce55-59ed-9737-6d8d550ca7da" :answer-field/key "$(Q∧P)∨P$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472344} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01ebbeed-4011-5c20-8329-099623c6a19a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471679} {:answer/id #uuid "80b85ce7-9288-5196-9ed1-2686999ab115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01ebbeed-4011-5c20-8329-099623c6a19a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471679} :answer-field/id #uuid "0af81364-23c4-5f19-a803-b4f9c13fed2b" :answer-field/key "$P∨(Q∨P)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34117327-fd37-5989-b657-502be019389b" :question/math-academy-id "q-81721" :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $P?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nP∨(P∧Q)≡P.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement $P∨(Q∧P)$ is logically equivalent to $P.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∨(Q∧P) & ≡P∨(P∧Q) \\\\  & ≡P.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement $(Q∧P)∨P$ is logically equivalent to $P.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(Q∧P)∨P & ≡P∨(Q∧P) \\\\  & ≡P∨(P∧Q) \\\\  & ≡P.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement $P∨(Q∨P)$ is *not* logically equivalent to $P.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P∨(Q∧P)$; $(Q∧P)∨P$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d4ea352-2a82-5ff5-8c08-b7f9a09929e6" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Disjunction Absorbs Conjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4d10fab-4103-56ce-8e7f-d0eedf9ab037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471681} {:answer/id #uuid "965d7134-25d2-535a-9052-64bd7c64c519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4d10fab-4103-56ce-8e7f-d0eedf9ab037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471681} :answer-field/id #uuid "655867d1-3c65-5e05-970d-802f9eb7191a" :answer-field/key "$M∨(N∨M)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472346} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e0cef47-9efb-570c-b54e-45245be3087d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471683} {:answer/id #uuid "fb8cb4a8-5040-5160-90c4-5362d6d30938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb8cb4a8-5040-5160-90c4-5362d6d30938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471684} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a4efad8-169e-5146-8833-f9b9c1343584" :answer-field/key "$(M∧N)∨M$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472347} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc4fca62-200c-5102-abbd-df4f9fb5f773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471685} {:answer/id #uuid "ce526e54-bf18-5d89-a1a2-6581d812eced" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce526e54-bf18-5d89-a1a2-6581d812eced" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471686} :answer-field/id #uuid "abe09b33-73e1-5d48-a50b-f6511ccdf629" :answer-field/key "$M∨(N∧M)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c524db33-b009-501a-aa7b-2de183456b8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-81722" :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $M?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nM∨(M∧N)≡M.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement $M∨(N∨M)$ is *not* logically equivalent to $M.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement $(M∧N)∨M$ is logically equivalent to $M.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(M∧N)∨M & ≡M∨(M∧N) \\\\  & ≡M.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement $M∨(N∧M)$ is logically equivalent to $M.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M∨(N∧M) & ≡M∨(M∧N) \\\\  & ≡M.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $(M∧N)∨M$; $M∨(N∧M)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a995511-c3ab-56a2-a302-1bedfa2904eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471747} {:answer/id #uuid "6107507d-d229-5b6d-bb78-6dd1692778b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6107507d-d229-5b6d-bb78-6dd1692778b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471748} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd7e4d8b-e538-50ff-8391-7016b9eb8aa4" :answer-field/key "If I am not awake, then I am sleeping." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a56ffb3-32e1-5ba6-b9d2-390da306e6c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471749} {:answer/id #uuid "daaaceb5-1235-586b-9abe-50131f6df41e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a56ffb3-32e1-5ba6-b9d2-390da306e6c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471749} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b29eaa7-fd58-579d-814b-190372ed2a71" :answer-field/key "If I am sleeping, then I am not awake." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472380} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dbda4a9-a5b8-5487-bcc5-bf76150369a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471751} {:answer/id #uuid "cfc52945-efa3-5eae-946e-3e2073cc7990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dbda4a9-a5b8-5487-bcc5-bf76150369a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471751} :answer-field/id #uuid "462f3da3-0d78-500c-8d71-92f10c5cbc0a" :answer-field/key "If I am awake, then I am not sleeping." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7b3cb87d-282a-5d16-9402-d3db5936c8ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-82660" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** I am not sleeping, **then** I am awake.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive.\n\n- Statement “If I am not awake, then I am sleeping” is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement “If I am sleeping, then I am not awake” is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement “If I am awake, then I am not sleeping” is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If I am not awake, then I am sleeping” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dda9d468-becb-54e6-9d7c-a36da59bbb0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471753} {:answer/id #uuid "3bc1de6b-6351-548e-b152-50fd8ef8413e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bc1de6b-6351-548e-b152-50fd8ef8413e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471754} :answer-field/id #uuid "a959e3ca-4163-50bd-9b6f-1b49bb7a3efb" :answer-field/key "If we do not watch a movie at home, then we go to the cinema." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472382} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "714898a2-3141-5053-ab51-02f399c94eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471755} {:answer/id #uuid "a436efc5-6bb5-5944-b3f8-595b5e63604d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "714898a2-3141-5053-ab51-02f399c94eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471755} :answer-field/id #uuid "18c69588-c464-5cab-89e1-7667dce161c6" :answer-field/key "If we watch a movie at home, then we do not go to the cinema." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472383} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39d3c8d9-8286-5656-ad84-dec522575e91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471757} {:answer/id #uuid "c0099cb5-5210-539d-8a9c-36530f395a74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39d3c8d9-8286-5656-ad84-dec522575e91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471757} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a7a2082-751e-5b23-942c-7a7417ba6a57" :answer-field/key "If we go to the cinema, then we do not watch a movie at home." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b3c08af-1740-5428-a4c7-1f507e3193d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-82664" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** we do not go to the cinema, **then** we watch a movie at home.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive.\n\n- Statement “If we do not watch a movie at home, then we go to the cinema” is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement “If we do not watch a movie at home, then we go to the cinema” is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement “If we go to the cinema, then we do not watch a movie at home” is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If we do not watch a movie at home, then we go to the cinema” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380284 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb97b679-ed73-5d50-b8f3-ebd938a5c69b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454138} {:answer/id #uuid "e3090b39-70db-561b-9774-7f4d38196900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3090b39-70db-561b-9774-7f4d38196900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454139} :answer-field/id #uuid "80e1f700-4e27-590e-9aea-505c9d96d52c" :answer-field/key "$H$ is closed under matrix addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454819} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b77c043e-6368-5cf0-87ba-b422015be2c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454140} {:answer/id #uuid "b7139452-025b-5bbb-8b6c-fac373d52ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7139452-025b-5bbb-8b6c-fac373d52ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454141} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b0eb3f5-b781-5609-babf-762a182d38c4" :answer-field/key "$H$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "530ae441-da27-537e-a55c-72a1a7eaffa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454142} {:answer/id #uuid "42ec41b7-fdfa-5e73-8caa-ca0e1481cad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42ec41b7-fdfa-5e73-8caa-ca0e1481cad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454143} :answer-field/id #uuid "f69bf366-d3cc-56cd-81b4-3fe0b32a22ef" :answer-field/key "$H$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53896f78-ec62-5396-8624-7b1c6badc360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454144} {:answer/id #uuid "74d6078b-e09a-5835-921b-48b69ffd8255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53896f78-ec62-5396-8624-7b1c6badc360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454144} :answer-field/id #uuid "57276cd0-38fc-5c29-abd0-eff90122f7d4" :answer-field/key "$H$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e8696fa-a30e-5b2e-a6f9-20152471933a" :question/math-academy-id "q-94621" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R,$ and its subset $H$ containing all $2\\times 2$ matrices such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $0.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$H$ is closed under matrix addition” is true. If ${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ are two matrices from $H$ such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $0,$ then \n\n$$\n{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}\n$$\n\n is a matrix where the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to \n\n$$\n0+0=0.\n$$\n\n This matrix belongs to $H.$ So, $H$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement “$H$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is true. If $A$ is an element of $H$ such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to $0,$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\nkA\n$$\n\n is a matrix such that the sum of the elements on the main diagonal is equal to \n\n$$\n0\\cdot k=0.\n$$\n\n This matrix belongs to $H.$ So, $H$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$H$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is true, while statement “$H$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is false. $H$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$H$ is closed under matrix addition”; “$H$ is closed under scalar multiplication”; “$H$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380291 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f077c77-0570-536a-a8a6-0a63cf4d87ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454146} {:answer/id #uuid "ef1ea41f-315c-59a7-b182-4abf0e4b7b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef1ea41f-315c-59a7-b182-4abf0e4b7b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454147} :answer-field/id #uuid "08b59da7-192e-5638-a6d9-30b5ec427b19" :answer-field/key "$D$ is closed under matrix addition" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9224e5e7-ecbe-5a8e-8ff9-aa2feb99653b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454148} {:answer/id #uuid "3146b088-175e-5e2a-8f28-d752332c1825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9224e5e7-ecbe-5a8e-8ff9-aa2feb99653b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454148} :answer-field/id #uuid "a160776e-c9a6-54ab-ba04-03293503bfa9" :answer-field/key "$D$ is closed under scalar multiplication" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3af3f92e-2bb3-5d0b-b1d2-d97e3317a680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454150} {:answer/id #uuid "2c6f3468-8a4e-525c-91f1-9eb0300f4e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3af3f92e-2bb3-5d0b-b1d2-d97e3317a680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454150} :answer-field/id #uuid "de85e3af-f485-549e-af6a-03e3f37ec071" :answer-field/key "$D$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454825} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "437f3bf2-f29e-5af5-aed6-837e31083c5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454152} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e8c9d8-9e82-5680-a3c9-bb84c07c77d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1e8c9d8-9e82-5680-a3c9-bb84c07c77d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454153} :answer-field/id #uuid "82587102-0923-537e-9e88-86ad077d77a6" :answer-field/key "$D$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02488e4e-8845-5c5e-a156-a562e8b67a01" :question/math-academy-id "q-94627" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $D={\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a<0}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$D$ is closed under matrix addition” is true. If ${A}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ are two matrices from $D,$ then  ${a}_{1}<0$ and ${a}_{2}<0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n is a matrix from $D,$ since ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}<0.$ So, $D$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement “$D$ is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. For example,  if $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $k=-1,$ then $A$ is an element of $D$ and $k\\in R,$ but \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =(-1)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis *not* in  $D.$ So, $D$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement “$D$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is false, while statement “$D$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” is true. $D$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$D$ is closed under matrix addition”; “$D$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380325 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124528 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20a6c0cf-04d4-5908-a03f-1adf491b9282" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60987df5-8c3c-54ae-838c-cd701fb442dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471789} {:answer/id #uuid "8f001032-df56-5a30-a156-b43b6ff775fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f001032-df56-5a30-a156-b43b6ff775fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471790} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a388f01-4a46-5643-acde-373829d0e415" :answer-field/key "${\\lambda }^{3}-4\\lambda =0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472400} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c598417-054a-57eb-b548-de0798c7d570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471791} {:answer/id #uuid "0b8aaebf-d279-5803-83a3-bd17d7899f6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c598417-054a-57eb-b548-de0798c7d570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471791} :answer-field/id #uuid "297b34f9-4160-5f88-8408-a21af344a053" :answer-field/key "${\\lambda }^{3}-3{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +4=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472401} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55ae7047-3b7e-51d5-9be1-7e2f66eecf5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471793} {:answer/id #uuid "d9fb77f4-4254-5c73-953b-7f787e0f61d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9fb77f4-4254-5c73-953b-7f787e0f61d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471794} :answer-field/id #uuid "74391771-4e6a-57d2-9134-21c7fb4ea916" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda (\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -1)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f94c3089-795c-58b5-a020-124bd7b98fb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-97859" :question/problem "If $B$ is a $3\\times 3$ non-invertible matrix, then which of the following could be the characteristic equation of $B?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ is non-invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, $0$ must be an eigenvalue of $B.$ As a result, $\\lambda =0$ should be a solution to the corresponding characteristic equation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given equations in turn.\n\n- Equation ${\\lambda }^{3}-4\\lambda =0$ could be the characteristic equation of $B.$ Indeed, $\\lambda =0$ is a root of the equation.\n\n- Equation ${\\lambda }^{3}-3{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +4=0$ **cannot** be the characteristic equation of $B$ since $\\lambda =0$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Equation $\\lambda (\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -1)=0$ could be the characteristic equation of $B.$ Indeed, $\\lambda =0$ is a root of the equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\lambda }^{3}-4\\lambda =0$; $\\lambda (\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -1)=0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380338 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124605 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c34e7d59-6bb4-5c2f-808f-212503d55338" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b62692e4-70a9-5b64-b572-8e95101f299d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454262} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f96054-430f-5abb-9738-492912b4513f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2f96054-430f-5abb-9738-492912b4513f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454263} :answer-field/id #uuid "52fb6fd8-12c2-5a40-95db-e8d434005870" :answer-field/key "$(B+2I)x=0$ has a nonzero solution" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454881} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43234e8f-f0ca-5794-8734-537c4540ced4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454264} {:answer/id #uuid "aea27afc-4d53-57d1-a1a6-faf52d441711" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aea27afc-4d53-57d1-a1a6-faf52d441711" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454265} :answer-field/id #uuid "f38bf0d7-cb37-587a-8201-a3fd186776a4" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(B+2I)\\ne {R}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f198704-9c2b-52ba-ab29-315f0f4f7390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454266} {:answer/id #uuid "356b12b2-b30c-58ef-898f-2e04dbb2332f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "356b12b2-b30c-58ef-898f-2e04dbb2332f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454267} :answer-field/id #uuid "d51aab6a-c250-5230-a3e0-85d81f4fb26b" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(B+2I)\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2cf92ef9-ce4a-5cbb-9e9d-9e8a2989e53d" :question/math-academy-id "q-97944" :question/problem "If $B$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\lambda =-2$ is an eigenvalue of $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a $3\\times 3$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=3=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nLet's now apply the theorem to the matrix $M=B+2I.$\n\n- Statement “$(B+2I)x=0$ has a nonzero solution” is true. Notice that if $\\lambda =-2$ is an eigenvalue of $B,$ then the nonzero solutions of $(B+2I)x=0$ are eigenvectors of $B.$ As a result, the matrix $M=B+2I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statements $\\text{Col}(B+2I)\\ne {R}^{3}$ and $\\text{nullity}(B+2I)\\ne 0$ are true. Since $M=B+2I$ is singular, by the invertible matrix theorem, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\text{Col}(B+2I)\\ne {R}^{3},\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(B+2I)\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$(B+2I)x=0$ has a nonzero solution”; $\\text{Col}(B+2I)\\ne {R}^{3}$; $\\text{nullity}(B+2I)\\ne 0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380345 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124605 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c34e7d59-6bb4-5c2f-808f-212503d55338" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a8febcf-d8f8-5bb1-bd0f-5ea5157901db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454268} {:answer/id #uuid "0d0ab0d9-c27a-5f5c-af64-9667450caa58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a8febcf-d8f8-5bb1-bd0f-5ea5157901db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454268} :answer-field/id #uuid "8384c379-0806-5ddf-b3d0-e3b82670fa9b" :answer-field/key "$(C-2I)x=0$ has only zero solution" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26764f15-21bd-5865-b436-a36b9b696003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454270} {:answer/id #uuid "a796bded-1ab7-53dd-8b24-5a4f06d7d263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a796bded-1ab7-53dd-8b24-5a4f06d7d263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454271} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a6693f4-1188-5c06-b9f9-4c671b8a0599" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(C-2I)\\ne {R}^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454885} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f7d45de-1453-5098-a4a6-edffb970d0d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454272} {:answer/id #uuid "89362b6b-2fd1-52b4-a6a5-5b6f4d773b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89362b6b-2fd1-52b4-a6a5-5b6f4d773b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454273} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ba61e62-3f3b-5078-93dc-7f400ec2f0c3" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Null}(C-2I)\\ne {0}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f636785f-61ec-504d-b842-394a5a79199b" :question/math-academy-id "q-97947" :question/problem "If $C$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a $4\\times 4$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=4=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nLet's now apply the theorem to the matrix $M=C-2I.$\n\n- Statement “$(C-2I)x=0$ has only zero solution” is false. Notice that if $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $C,$ then the nonzero solutions of $(C-2I)x=0$ are eigenvectors of $C.$ As a result, the matrix $M=C-2I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statements $\\text{Col}(C-2I)\\ne {R}^{4}$ and $\\text{Null}(C-2I)\\ne {0}$ are true. Since $M=C-2I$ is singular, by the invertible matrix theorem, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\text{Col}(C-2I)\\ne {R}^{4},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(C-2I)\\ne {0}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{Col}(C-2I)\\ne {R}^{4}$; $\\text{Null}(C-2I)\\ne {0}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124529 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d1a3a3-a6f0-522c-9161-6dc0fefb2e0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix and Rank-Nullity Theorems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f28abe1-7ce7-5fcd-800c-5355d28b4dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454274} {:answer/id #uuid "975b6d1f-67e4-5ad0-a60c-f212c150bba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "975b6d1f-67e4-5ad0-a60c-f212c150bba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454275} :answer-field/id #uuid "01e4ad4b-797b-5e1c-957c-e3b4e3622e5b" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(B-2I)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b268ef17-aa66-5222-b880-47a780072089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454276} {:answer/id #uuid "98e68f38-5fa0-5696-a788-a965baf32116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b268ef17-aa66-5222-b880-47a780072089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454276} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec0d8911-05a3-5867-85d8-d03e8d8a263a" :answer-field/key "$B-2I$ is non-singular" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454888} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9e6411f-f645-554b-849c-9e1f5f16f32f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454278} {:answer/id #uuid "0df6ff7c-41ab-51b6-a2ff-1f6813596ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0df6ff7c-41ab-51b6-a2ff-1f6813596ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454279} :answer-field/id #uuid "8031e5cb-78c7-579e-9e68-cf112703c2a4" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a33206bb-7969-5524-a745-290fffeff16f" :question/math-academy-id "q-97967" :question/problem "If $B$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(B-2I)=3,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a $4\\times 4$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=4=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $M$ has $4$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(M)+\\text{nullity}(M)=4.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{nullity}(B-2I)=1$ is true. According to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(B-2I) & =4-\\text{rank}(B-2I) \\\\  & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statements “$B-2I$ is non-singular” is false. By the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(B-2I)\\ne 0,$ we obtain that $B-2I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statement “$\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $B$” is true. Notice that if $M=B-2I$ is singular, then $(B-2I)x=0$ has nonzero solutions which will be eigenvectors of $B.$ As a result, $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{nullity}(B-2I)=1$; “$\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $B$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "337518a9-39a1-57e3-8686-74a135f7c3d7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Oriented Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "666f635f-2d2c-58d1-a88c-b86e8e2df780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471795} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ac7c63-65b4-5309-ae76-0fdcf97d72bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "666f635f-2d2c-58d1-a88c-b86e8e2df780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471795} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eb108e6-8c9b-5a85-b513-2e65c9b9014f" :answer-field/key "![Curve I](images/11/11b213b12d3699320aebd4c6fe40498810a2709d69dcb333f9bf1703486bf723.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472403} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b63367f-8102-5a8e-a9aa-c17faba2a0a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471797} {:answer/id #uuid "04c05a69-436a-5a0f-8693-f7ee5315f726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b63367f-8102-5a8e-a9aa-c17faba2a0a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471797} :answer-field/id #uuid "07e7680b-3320-5700-ac48-cb843a65d006" :answer-field/key "![Curve II](images/5f/5ff5c37838aad543170f6bbe0c7b47936333713df44a5e27e4df95574219cf1b.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472404} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad6c7bfc-6af9-576e-bb3c-4cd74d40aee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471799} {:answer/id #uuid "222305a5-edff-552c-a29c-a72602b1be77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "222305a5-edff-552c-a29c-a72602b1be77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471800} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c84ef73-0379-56c5-897a-2e57bbb94116" :answer-field/key "![Curve III](images/ed/ed952a218ecf01107161ce8cc6d8f4547102ed1b7bf23bec695e2d493ae2ed39.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472405} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ceb6c668-d138-5653-b3ab-7e1933dee240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471801} {:answer/id #uuid "967dfc80-0ccd-54fc-9cd0-0b3759c0ba32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceb6c668-d138-5653-b3ab-7e1933dee240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471801} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c5a7337-e66d-5281-80a2-b1471a252037" :answer-field/key "![Curve IV](images/ab/abd41a3c37e7841ea69e2c479207f464fb570da9677d869ff4064d5338609e01.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f035c68d-f32c-5e67-98cc-62c8475830d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-98341" :question/problem "Which of the curves below is simple, closed, and negatively oriented?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A simple closed curve is positively oriented if, when traveling along it, one always has the curve interior to the left and the curve exterior to the right. Otherwise, the curve is negatively oriented. \n\nA curve is positively oriented if it is traversed counterclockwise and is negatively oriented if it is traversed clockwise.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the curves:\n\n- Curve I is not closed.\n\n- Curve II is not simple.\n\n- Curve III is simple, closed, negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed clockwise.\n\n- Curve IV is a simple and closed curve but it is not negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed counterclockwise, so it is positively oriented.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is curve III only"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380393 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90f4b8b6-9087-5496-807d-608724aa78fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470631} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5fbf91-d7c1-5e8c-871e-7c26b0ac303e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb5fbf91-d7c1-5e8c-871e-7c26b0ac303e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470632} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b1dfa9f-9494-59d8-bf95-2c68f20b60a5" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6085786-4948-5140-96cc-351034d2e7a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470633} {:answer/id #uuid "4fce3179-81d2-55bd-a37c-d2f3b28beee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fce3179-81d2-55bd-a37c-d2f3b28beee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470634} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffaaf373-8b01-5dda-82d5-b55d324b703d" :answer-field/key "${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471822} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fecb31b-eea1-5984-a868-c589f3e59e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470635} {:answer/id #uuid "0b89d20b-e663-5580-8552-4bead320d1f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fecb31b-eea1-5984-a868-c589f3e59e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470635} :answer-field/id #uuid "a51c31a2-df0f-5d9f-bff0-d622cce2a150" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb972e63-3e46-543b-9a40-0120a6183656" :question/math-academy-id "q-100120" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t-4,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=2-t,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=1-t.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(1)q(1)+p(2)q(2),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t-4,1-t⟩ \\\\  & =(2t-4){|}_{1}\\cdot (1-t){|}_{1}+(2t-4){|}_{2}\\cdot (1-t){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(2(1)-4)\\cdot (1-1)+(2(2)-4)\\cdot (1-2) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨2-t,1-t⟩ \\\\  & =(2-t){|}_{1}\\cdot (1-t){|}_{1}+(2-t){|}_{2}\\cdot (1-t){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(2-1)\\cdot (1-1)+(2-2)\\cdot (1-2) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Let's check if ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t).$ Computing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t-4,2-t⟩ \\\\  & =(2t-4){|}_{1}\\cdot (2-t){|}_{1}+(2t-4){|}_{2}\\cdot (2-t){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(2(1)-4)\\cdot (2-1)+(2(2)-4)\\cdot (2-2) \\\\  & =-2\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product. So, the set $S$ is *not* an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product”; “${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38977e25-5701-59b4-acd7-c07e28c73e8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470637} {:answer/id #uuid "795d2da5-60e6-5507-9355-3921ddc95792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "795d2da5-60e6-5507-9355-3921ddc95792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470638} :answer-field/id #uuid "c745d006-d5de-5a2f-9e45-1c00146eae2a" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4846a1f4-412a-515c-8ef9-ed21e5470f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470639} {:answer/id #uuid "e6594a2d-fafd-5fa9-8390-bc86bc6736e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4846a1f4-412a-515c-8ef9-ed21e5470f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470639} :answer-field/id #uuid "4afd9177-d9a1-52e6-9b31-5287eb0e1f1b" :answer-field/key "${p}_{2}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471825} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40c96296-fbc5-5ab2-9c9f-253e362d1483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470641} {:answer/id #uuid "95e9e5ba-829c-5853-bb9d-a29fdf02c6fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40c96296-fbc5-5ab2-9c9f-253e362d1483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470641} :answer-field/id #uuid "54703d9d-be5e-5e7e-ab6d-caae8559077f" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39aa7418-1a3f-5a9e-9642-6c49cf6dc36a" :question/math-academy-id "q-100129" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t+2,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t-2,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=t+1.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(2)q(2),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t+2,t-2⟩ \\\\  & =(2t+2){|}_{-1}\\cdot (t-2){|}_{-1}+(2t+2){|}_{2}\\cdot (t-2){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(2(-1)+2)\\cdot ((-1)-2)+(2(2)+2)\\cdot (2-2) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{2}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is false since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨t-2,t+1⟩ \\\\  & =(t-2){|}_{-1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{-1}+(t-2){|}_{2}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{2} \\\\  & =((-1)-2)\\cdot ((-1)+1)+(2-2)\\cdot (2+1) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Let's check if ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t).$ Computing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t+2,t+1⟩ \\\\  & =(2t+2){|}_{-1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{-1}+(2t+2){|}_{2}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(2(-1)+2)\\cdot ((-1)+1)+(2(2)+2)\\cdot (2+1) \\\\  & =18\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product. So, the set $S$ is *not* an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fe686b5-c7f0-58e6-9e46-e769a9193b21" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db71db57-8f3b-562d-aa65-e810d0b3a0be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470697} {:answer/id #uuid "fd595c08-94c2-5bae-a608-e1f0c371fa9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd595c08-94c2-5bae-a608-e1f0c371fa9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470698} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a911763-5020-50b9-9cb5-871677eea7a1" :answer-field/key "There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471854} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5641305d-3f75-589d-9901-64a5729ed81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470699} {:answer/id #uuid "256bd11d-8faa-55e9-82be-41d161248a64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "256bd11d-8faa-55e9-82be-41d161248a64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470700} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fb93a02-8501-5b93-b215-0594f7d2d818" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471855} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f9725a3-3382-56cb-adab-98f55021b84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470701} {:answer/id #uuid "b91be735-f96b-5a3d-a044-c0e9ff29f921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b91be735-f96b-5a3d-a044-c0e9ff29f921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470702} :answer-field/id #uuid "787ac8fe-cc26-50ca-b9d2-a10a864885f5" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471856}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "db140378-9b82-5420-9a09-f186b3b4c9b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-104956" :question/problem "![](images/8d/8d5a71c78a8e8aa5c4c17189a7e2fcf739af2b4e6d93819e87aa9f3f7135c8cd.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=4$” is true. According to the diagram, we have $f(1)=4$ (we have an arrow from $1\\in X$ to $4\\in Y$). So, there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=4.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$” is true. As we can see from the diagram, for all $y$ contained within $Y,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is true. Since statement “$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$” is true, $f$ is a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=4$”; “$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$”; “$f$ is a surjection”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380420 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fe686b5-c7f0-58e6-9e46-e769a9193b21" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84280041-92fd-5192-93c9-e48627a8d61d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470703} {:answer/id #uuid "f8d9c6cc-655d-587f-a7ea-5270008520aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84280041-92fd-5192-93c9-e48627a8d61d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470703} :answer-field/id #uuid "926a2635-c239-5abe-bfe8-8f19a21bad02" :answer-field/key "There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471857} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "550f969f-73eb-5d0d-a662-b666c5779497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470705} {:answer/id #uuid "a819f3f3-e7ac-55f9-b274-f932e5858b20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "550f969f-73eb-5d0d-a662-b666c5779497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470705} :answer-field/id #uuid "64b1381a-39d6-5006-bdce-409b33804a49" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471858} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afe2e275-0d80-52bd-87be-996bbe232db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470707} {:answer/id #uuid "196f578f-57fc-5e51-97d6-f6020044ee46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afe2e275-0d80-52bd-87be-996bbe232db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470707} :answer-field/id #uuid "44ab2c15-20df-54dd-b6fd-3f24203d3699" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7e09caa-cacf-54dd-ae93-0599cdfc3d85" :question/math-academy-id "q-104957" :question/problem "![](images/80/801bb98497bc275acda854447fffee30721bc54b2711ac632c2269f0c1eb64ed.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=-1$” is false. As we can see from the diagram, there are no elements contained within $X$ that have an arrow to $-1\\in Y.$ Hence, $f(x)\\ne -1$ for all $x\\in X.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false. Since statement “There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=-1$” is false,  it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $Y,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is false. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false, $f$ is not a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fe686b5-c7f0-58e6-9e46-e769a9193b21" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3e0f2a6-da32-5a3e-8038-89e24c09e272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470709} {:answer/id #uuid "ab3452d1-013a-53c5-a2de-57a2d9f941e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab3452d1-013a-53c5-a2de-57a2d9f941e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470710} :answer-field/id #uuid "f96f0323-da65-5381-9e93-1f8171c8674f" :answer-field/key "There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=7$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471860} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25f42b2a-d794-5b15-8036-dcc8c69bb940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470711} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1b2c33-3dfe-58e8-85c4-d8984d0d7ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25f42b2a-d794-5b15-8036-dcc8c69bb940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470711} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e50acad-18ff-5772-98c8-8e5ad8ee596a" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471861} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4de3c43-fec6-52f9-9554-a815044c92b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470713} {:answer/id #uuid "8d2a6bde-cbe6-5b08-8c2b-1712a8ec63b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4de3c43-fec6-52f9-9554-a815044c92b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470713} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c6bac77-ef1e-593d-badb-80ae667f1767" :answer-field/key "$f$ is **onto**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65240711-5d62-532c-a650-6596f72fcd4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-104959" :question/problem "![](images/94/94f14d4a1876588cbfb2abc4a1542d5961587745a6e24aeae270d15f75f834db.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=7$” is true. According to the diagram, we have $f(1)=7$ (we have an arrow from $2\\in X$ to $7\\in Y$). So, there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=7.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false. Consider $y=5.$ As we can see from the diagram, there are no elements contained within $X$ that have an arrow to $5\\in Y.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $Y,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **onto**” is false. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false, $f$ is not a surjection (also known as *onto*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=7$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152133 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63a2b195-d0b3-580c-9230-58533d86afd5" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Domain and Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6d9971d-5d83-5fb4-86e2-96890c06d6e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453138} {:answer/id #uuid "c4baccc4-826f-558c-ba91-c27ae92daa70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6d9971d-5d83-5fb4-86e2-96890c06d6e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453138} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d634da5-20ce-5fc9-9321-b86b451d7bcf" :answer-field/key "The range of $f$ is $[1,\\infty )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454319} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33c9a902-640a-526a-abef-206e