on. \n\n![](images/80/80630fae7c4f1e29d855e9a68917156ccf3ecbefd0efc7bda5a9bd0e903c90db.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The range of $f$ is $[1,\\infty )$” is false. The graph covers all $y$-values, so the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$” is true. Since the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty )$, then for all $y$ contained within $R,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **onto**” is true. Since statement “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$” is true, $f$ is a surjection of $R$ onto $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$”; “$f$ is **onto**” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380441 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1324fd0b-5388-5133-ad6a-72d658e3c903" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is a Real Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e28e4282-21e6-5a86-b20e-c7e629c93191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470715} {:answer/id #uuid "014ee5ee-8365-5944-a6a9-e810b48cfc76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "014ee5ee-8365-5944-a6a9-e810b48cfc76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470716} :answer-field/id #uuid "b50b6a19-4f09-5ebd-a5a0-de6e3bb517d1" :answer-field/key "The range of $f$ is $[-1,3]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471863} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea552826-dfdd-5fb2-9580-fc993db48941" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470717} {:answer/id #uuid "4d28a38f-86b5-5199-a603-19573a39e22d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d28a38f-86b5-5199-a603-19573a39e22d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470718} :answer-field/id #uuid "a95a14e0-febb-5d4f-8b82-6e52fbf2a6d9" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in [-1,3],$ $∃\\,x\\in [-1,5]$ such that $f(x)=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471864} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0c886db-64ae-5362-9827-ebecf741914b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470719} {:answer/id #uuid "ec457a17-fa71-54c0-ac26-1650cb283017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0c886db-64ae-5362-9827-ebecf741914b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470719} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7fb7f7f-b5d1-5f67-95c4-943fd00674ab" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f86e164-e19a-5fdd-bd77-619a454eb721" :question/math-academy-id "q-104973" :question/problem "![](images/94/94c9daf5f16776eef520e40f68a38dc5e05c4ceb5470cdc18880ac288a9ce031.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-1,5]\\to [-1,4]$ whose graph is shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The range of $f$ is $[-1,3]$” is true. From the graph, the highest $y$-value is $3$ and the lowest $y$-value is $-1.$ The graph covers all $y$-values between $-1$ and $3$, including these numbers, so the range of the function is $[-1,3].$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in [-1,3],$ $∃\\,x\\in [-1,5]$ such that $f(x)=y$” is true. Since the range of $f$ is $[-1,3]$ and $[-1,3]$ is contained in that range, it follows that for all $y$ contained within $[-1,3],$ there exists some $x$ contained within $[-1,5]$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is false. As we can see from the range, there is no real number $x$ such that $f(x)=4.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $[-1,4],$ there exists some $x$ contained within $[-1,5]$ such that $f(x)=y.$ In conclusion, $f$ is not a surjection of $[-1,5]$ onto $[-1,4].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The range of $f$ is $[-1,3]$”; “$∀\\,y\\in [-1,3],$ $∃\\,x\\in [-1,5]$ such that $f(x)=y$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1324fd0b-5388-5133-ad6a-72d658e3c903" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is a Real Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23f43283-9451-548d-9203-c8d8809918e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/va